window.DS3_CHUNK("spells",[{"id":"acid-surge","kind":"spell","name":"Acid Surge","page":"Acid Surge (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Acid_Surge__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"24","req":{"int":null,"fth":13},"buy":6000,"desc":"Pyromancy of Carthus of the Sands.\nEmits an acid which corrodes weapons and armor.\nCarthus' swordsmen attached great value to victory, and would not shun the use of such pyromancies. For where is the honor in death and scoured bones?","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 6,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"carthus-pyromancy-tome\">Carthus Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster spews a cloud of corrosive mist, which damages the durability of all applicable equipment of enemies caught within by about 2 points per second. Cloud persists for 5-6 seconds and moves forward from the caster upon cast, meaning that each cast has the potential to reduce target durability by up to 12 points.<\/p><p>The durability damage inflicted by Acid Surge cannot be mitigated by wearing the <a data-e=\"wood-grain-ring\">Wood Grain Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Acid_Surge_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"affinity","kind":"spell","name":"Affinity","page":"Affinity (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Affinity__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"40","req":{"int":32,"fth":null},"buy":15000,"desc":"A forbidden dark sorcery. Casts a dark manifestation of humanity.\nIt appears to be an expression of envy, or perhaps love towards another, that will tenaciously pursue its target. Even if, like so many human desires, it amounts to nothing but misfortune.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 15,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures up five orbs around the caster, similar to <a data-e=\"homing-soulmass\">Homing Soulmass<\/a>. When an enemy within the caster's frontal arc gets close enough, the orbs lock on and slowly chase the target, with each orb capable of dealing 0.6 times the Spell Buff of the wielded catalyst as Dark damage upon impact. If the orbs collide with any level geometry without flying at a target, they will automatically explode.<\/p><p>As with other Dark Sorceries, this spell is subject to having its power boosted by wielding the proper catalyst.<\/p><p>Unlike Homing Soulmass and <a data-e=\"homing-crystal-soulmass\">Homing Crystal Soulmass<\/a>, the number of orbs conjured is always 5, regardless of the caster's Intelligence.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Affinity_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"atonement","kind":"spell","name":"Atonement","page":"Atonement","img":"assets/img/Atonement.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":null,"fth":18},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle given to those cast out from the Sable Church of Londor.\nAttracts more attention from foes.\nThis is the only tale known by exiles, who believe it carries words of forgiveness. Cursed journeys, too, must come to an end.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep Perimeter<\/a> bonfire, turn around and head further into the ruins. Look for a hole on the right wall and drop through it. The spell can be looted from a nearby corpse, along with another holding a <a data-e=\"hollow-gem\">Hollow Gem<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases the enemies' aggro range toward the player. Lasts for 30 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Atonement"},{"id":"aural-decoy","kind":"spell","name":"Aural Decoy","page":"Aural Decoy (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Aural_Decoy__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":2000,"desc":"Sorcery developed by a certain surreptitious\nsorcerer at Vinheim Dragon School.\nDistracts foes with a distant sound.\nThe sound carries with it a strangely infectious\nresonance that may cause one to stray from their\npost and expose their back.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 2,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures an orb that flies in the casting direction. Once the orb hits solid level geometry or travels its maximum distance, it will produce running sounds, distracting any nearby enemies and causing them to face the source of the sound. The orb will produce sound for 3 seconds before vanishing.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Aural_Decoy_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-fire-orb","kind":"spell","name":"Black Fire Orb","page":"Black Fire Orb","img":"assets/img/Black_Fire_Orb.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"22","req":{"int":20,"fth":20},"buy":10000,"desc":"Pyromancy discovered by grave wardens after High Lord Wolnir fell to the Abyss.\nHurls a black fireball.\nThe black flame inflicts dark damage, striking targets with weighty force.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 10,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"grave-warden-pyromancy-tome\">Grave Warden Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Hurls a black fireball at the target, inflicting 2.4 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage. Enemies caught in the explosion at the impact point rather than being hit by the fireball itself will take only 2.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Fire_Orb"},{"id":"black-flame","kind":"spell","name":"Black Flame","page":"Black Flame (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Black_Flame__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":15,"fth":15},"buy":10000,"desc":"Pyromancy discovered by grave wardens after High Lord Wolnir fell to the Abyss.\nCreates a giant, black flame in hand.\nBlack flames born from the Abyss bear no shadow. They are said to be the impenetrable fires of humanity.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 10,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"grave-warden-pyromancy-tome\">Grave Warden Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a dark explosion from the palm of the caster's hand, inflicting 2.4 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage. If a target is only caught in the flames lingering after the initial explosion, they will take only 2.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Flame_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"black-serpent","kind":"spell","name":"Black Serpent","page":"Black Serpent","img":"assets/img/Black_Serpent.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"19","req":{"int":15,"fth":15},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancy discovered from the Abyss by High Lord Wolnir that inspired the black arts of the grave wardens.\nReleases undulating black flames that trace the ground.\nBe it sorcery or pyromancy, all techniques that infringe on humanity lead to the same place. That is to say, they all seek a will of their own.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-high-lord-wolnir\">Soul of High Lord Wolnir<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a rippling black flame at their feet that surges forward and weaves across the ground, tracking on the locked-on target. Has minor homing capability, and inflicts 1.65 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage to enemies it passes through.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-high-lord-wolnir","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Serpent"},{"id":"blessed-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Blessed Weapon","page":"Blessed Weapon","img":"assets/img/Blessed_Weapon.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"35","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":8000,"desc":"Miracle taught to Lothric Knights.\nBlesses right weapon, increasing attack power, as well as gradually restoring HP.\nThe Knight is one of the Three Pillars of Lothric, said to have strengthened ties with the High Priestess after the Scholars acquired the Grand Archives.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 8,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-lothric\">Braille Divine Tome of Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Buffs right-hand weapon, increasing Physical damage by 7.5%, and also gradually restoring HP for 45 seconds. The HP restored per second is 1 for every 50 Spell Buff of the casting tool used.<\/p><p>Additionally, the weapon gains the same properties as a <a data-e=\"blessed-gem\">Blessed<\/a>-infused weapon, in that it will deal bonus damage to skeletons and prevent them from reviving.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Blessed_Weapon"},{"id":"boulder-heave","kind":"spell","name":"Boulder Heave","page":"Boulder Heave","img":"assets/img/Boulder_Heave.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"17","req":{"int":8,"fth":12},"buy":null,"desc":"Art of a stray demon of stifled flame.\nSpews a boulder from one's mouth.\nThe boulder is heavy, but shatters easily.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-stray-demon\">Soul of a Stray Demon<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 0 souls.<\/p>","use":"","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-a-stray-demon","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Boulder_Heave"},{"id":"bountiful-light","kind":"spell","name":"Bountiful Light","page":"Bountiful Light","img":"assets/img/Bountiful_Light.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"45","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":5000,"desc":"Miracle taught to knights of Gertrude, holy maiden to the Queen.\nGradually restores a large amount of HP.\nThe Heavenly Daughter is said to be the Queen's child.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 5,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-lothric\">Braille Divine Tome of Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores 7 HP per second for 58-59 seconds, for a total of 406-413 HP.<\/p><p>The duration of the heal, and thus amount of HP recovered, cannot be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Bountiful_Light"},{"id":"bountiful-sunlight","kind":"spell","name":"Bountiful Sunlight","page":"Bountiful Sunlight (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Bountiful_Sunlight__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"70","req":{"int":null,"fth":35},"buy":null,"desc":"Special Miracle granted by the Princess of Sunlight.\nGradually restores a large amount of HP for self and those in the vicinity.\nThe miracles of Gwynevere, loved as both mother and wife, bestow their blessing on a great many warriors.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-rosaria\">Soul of Rosaria<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 0 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores 10 HP per second for 58-59 seconds, for a total of 580-590 HP, for caster and all nearby allies.<\/p><p>The duration of the heal can be extended by using the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>, but this only decreases the rate at which the spell heals with no effect on the total amount healed.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-rosaria","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Bountiful_Sunlight_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"bursting-fireball","kind":"spell","name":"Bursting Fireball","page":"Bursting Fireball","img":"assets/img/Bursting_Fireball.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"14","req":{"int":18,"fth":12},"buy":5000,"desc":"Pyromancy of old restored by Cornyx. One of the Great Swamp's more advanced spells.\nHurls an exploding fireball.\nA rare technique that undergoes change after leaving the caster's hand, making this a spell renowned for its difficulty.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 5,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome\">Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Throws a fireball that immediately splits into 11 smaller splinters, which spread out in a fan in front of the caster. Each splinter inflicts 0.71 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage to any enemies caught, and multiple splinters can hit the same target.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Bursting_Fireball"},{"id":"caressing-tears","kind":"spell","name":"Caressing Tears","page":"Caressing Tears","img":"assets/img/Caressing_Tears.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"14","req":{"int":null,"fth":12},"buy":1500,"desc":"Miracle taught by Morne, the Archbishop's apostle.\nCures bleed, poison, and frost for self and those in the vicinity.\nCaressing Tears is a tale of the many deaths surrounding the goddess Caitha, of whom Morne was a known follower.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 1,500 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Cures Bleed, Poison, Toxic and Frost for self and those in the vicinity. Also removes buildup of the above status effects if they have not procced.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Caressing_Tears"},{"id":"carthus-beacon","kind":"spell","name":"Carthus Beacon","page":"Carthus Beacon","img":"assets/img/Carthus_Beacon.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":2,"fp":"35","req":{"int":12,"fth":12},"buy":8000,"desc":"The most obscure pyromancy developed in Carthus of the Sands.\nDamage increases with consecutive attacks.\nCarthus's aggression has been likened to an uncontrollable fire, and since ancient times its beacon has been used as a signal for war.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 8,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"carthus-pyromancy-tome\">Carthus Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Damage increases by 7-15% with consecutive attacks, as long as attacking persists and is not interrupted. The base effect works on spells but the further damage increase does not.<\/p><p>Buff lasts for 30 seconds and does not stack with <a data-e=\"power-within\">Power Within<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Carthus_Beacon"},{"id":"carthus-flame-arc","kind":"spell","name":"Carthus Flame Arc","page":"Carthus Flame Arc","img":"assets/img/Carthus_Flame_Arc.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":10,"fth":10},"buy":10000,"desc":"Pyromancy of Carthus of the Sands. Reinforces right weapon with flame.\nWarriors of Carthus favored supplemental pyromancies such as this, which was used to enhance the curved blades of its swordsmen.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 10,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"carthus-pyromancy-tome\">Carthus Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces right-hand weapon with Fire. Added damage is dependent on the Spell Buff rating of the tool used, and is not affected by spell-boosting rings like the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-ring\">Great Swamp Ring<\/a>:<\/p><table><tr><th>Spell Buff<\/th><th>Conversion Efficiency<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>100-115<\/td><td>80%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>116-124<\/td><td>81%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>125-144<\/td><td>82%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>145-150<\/td><td>83%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>151-165<\/td><td>84%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>166-171<\/td><td>85%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>172-174<\/td><td>86%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>175-182<\/td><td>87%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>183-188<\/td><td>88%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>189-196<\/td><td>89%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>197-203<\/td><td>90%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>204-208<\/td><td>91%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>209-216<\/td><td>92%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>217-221<\/td><td>93%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>222-227<\/td><td>94%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>228-233<\/td><td>95%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>234-240<\/td><td>96%<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>241-242<\/td><td>97%<\/td><\/tr><\/table><p>Base duration of the buff is 90 seconds, which can be increased via equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Carthus_Flame_Arc"},{"id":"cast-light","kind":"spell","name":"Cast Light","page":"Cast Light (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Cast_Light__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":1000,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden Sorceries. Casts a light to illuminate surroundings.\nThis light producing magic is elementary, but nonetheless demonstrates the pure nature of golden sorceries; the likes of which have not been developed even at the Dragon School.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 1,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a glowing orb above the caster's head. The orb persists for 60 seconds, and the duration can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>. <br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Cast_Light_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"chameleon","kind":"spell","name":"Chameleon","page":"Chameleon (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Chameleon__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":12,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden sorceries. Transforms into something inconspicuous.\nFar from formally developed, this magic was instead born from the mischief of a young girl who sought relief from the solitude of the woods at dusk.","avail":"<p>Can be obtained in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a> by any of the following sources:<\/p><ul><li>Dropped by the <a data-e=\"old-woman-of-londor\">Old Woman of Londor<\/a> in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Church of Yorshka<\/a>. If following <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri<\/a>'s questline, an additional statue will appear at the back-left corner of the church, among many others. Hitting it will reveal it to be a pilgrim concealed by using this same spell.<\/li><li>Found on the <a data-e=\"old-woman-of-londor\">Old Woman of Londor<\/a>'s dead body in the Darkmoon Tomb behind an illusory wall, just before arriving to <a data-e=\"anor-londo\">Anor Londo<\/a>. Requires the player to proceed though <a data-e=\"anri-of-astora\">Anri<\/a>'s questline for the body to appear.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Transforms the caster into an inconspicuous object that blends with the environment. While transformed, the caster can change equipment and switch weapons without breaking camouflage, though attacking,, getting attacked, using items, interacting with the world or gesturing will cause the transformation to end. Movement is reduced to walking speed, and dropping off a ledge of any height will break the illusion.<\/p><p>Chameleon can transform the caster into the following objects:<\/p><h4>Cemetery of Ash and Untended Graves<\/h4><ul><li>Large tombstone<\/li><li>Small headstone<\/li><\/ul><h4>High Wall of Lothric and Consumed King's Garden<\/h4><ul><li>Barrel<\/li><li>Candle-holding praying statue (lit candle)<\/li><li>Headless Lothric Knight armor (from the Winged Knight courtyard onward)<\/li><\/ul><h4>Undead Settlement<\/h4><ul><li>Cage Spider<\/li><li>Tree-headed corpse<\/li><li>Covered pot<\/li><\/ul><h4>Road of Sacrifices<\/h4><ul><li>Box crate<\/li><li>Circular short crucifix<\/li><li>Chained three-pronged crucifix<\/li><\/ul><h4>Farron Keep<\/h4><ul><li>Box crate<\/li><li>Circular short crucifix<\/li><li>Rotting Ghru crucifix<\/li><\/ul><h4>Cathedral of the Deep<\/h4><p>Cathedral exterior:<\/p><ul><li>Box crate<\/li><li>Large tombstone<\/li><li>Short urn ornament<\/li><\/ul><p>Cathedral interior:<\/p><ul><li>Chair<\/li><li>Stooping hollow statue<\/li><li>Mourning woman statue<\/li><\/ul><h4>Catacombs of Carthus<\/h4><ul><li>Bone-filled small urn<\/li><li>Bone-filled tall urn<\/li><li>Covered powder barrel<\/li><\/ul><h4>Smouldering Lake<\/h4><ul><li>Demon Statue on pedestal<\/li><li>Covered powder barrel<\/li><\/ul><h4>Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/h4><ul><li>Small stooping priest statue<\/li><li>Silver Knight Straight Sword-holding squire statue<\/li><\/ul><h4>Anor Londo<\/h4><ul><li>Sword-holding Silver Knight statue<\/li><\/ul><h4>Irithyll Dungeon and Profaned Capital<\/h4><ul><li>Tall-backed chair<\/li><li>Aristocrat's Mask<\/li><\/ul><h4>Lothric Castle<\/h4><ul><li>Ornate wooden chair<\/li><li>Unlit candelabrum<\/li><li>Wooden box<\/li><\/ul><h4>Grand Archives<\/h4><p>Archives exterior:<\/p><ul><li>Crown-wearing gargoyle<\/li><\/ul><p>Archives interior:<\/p><ul><li>Armillary sphere<\/li><li>Wooden lectern<\/li><\/ul><h4>Archdragon Peak<\/h4><ul><li>Broken pillar<\/li><li>Short Nameless King statue<\/li><li>Path of the Dragon male <a data-e=\"dragon-torso-stone\">pseudo-dragon<\/a> statue<\/li><\/ul><h4>Kiln of the First Flame<\/h4><ul><li>Flame-scorched pillar<\/li><li>Large tombstone<\/li><\/ul><h4>Painted World of Ariandel<\/h4><p>Snowfield, Rope Bridge Cave, Snowy Mountain Pass:<\/p><ul><li>Birch Woman<\/li><li>Medium-height tree<\/li><\/ul><p>Corvian Settlement:<\/p><ul><li>Destroyed woman statue<\/li><li>Medium white tombstone<\/li><li>Wooden box<\/li><\/ul><p>Ariandel Chapel:<\/p><ul><li>Short stepladder<\/li><li>Wooden box<\/li><li>Wooden chair<\/li><\/ul><p>Depths of the Painting:<\/p><ul><li>Snow-covered rock<\/li><\/ul><h4>The Dreg Heap<\/h4><p>Upper Dreg Heap:<\/p><ul><li>Headless Lothric Knight armor<\/li><li>Londor Pilgrim<\/li><li>Wooden crate<\/li><\/ul><p>Earthen Peak:<\/p><ul><li>Large stone block<\/li><li>Londor Pilgrim<\/li><li>Wooden crate<\/li><\/ul><h4>The Ringed City<\/h4><p>Mausoleum Lookout:<\/p><ul><li>Hollow mausoleum tombstone<\/li><li>Small covered pot<\/li><li><a data-e=\"sword-of-avowal\">Sword of Avowal<\/a> statue<\/li><\/ul><p>Upper Ringed City, Shared Grave, Church of Filianore:<\/p><ul><li><a data-e=\"ringed-knight-spear\">Spear<\/a>-wielding Ringed Knight statue<\/li><li>Small covered pot<\/li><li>Sword of Avowal statue<\/li><\/ul><p>Ringed city swamp:<\/p><ul><li>Dark crystal growth<\/li><li>Humanity Phantom (only within the swamp itself)<\/li><li>Small covered pot<\/li><li>Spear-wielding Ringed Knight statue<\/li><li>Sword of Avowal statue<\/li><\/ul><p>Pygmy's Throne:<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Chameleon_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"chaos-bed-vestiges","kind":"spell","name":"Chaos Bed Vestiges","page":"Chaos Bed Vestiges","img":"assets/img/Chaos_Bed_Vestiges.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":2,"fp":"35","req":{"int":20,"fth":10},"buy":5000,"desc":"Traces of the tumultuous seedbed that birthed the beings known as Demons.\nHurls chaos flame that scorches vicinity.\nDemons born from fire bore its smoldering essence and perished soon after. Man shares this rapport with the flames to this day.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-old-demon-king\">Soul of the Old Demon King<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 5,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>If this spell hits directly, it causes great damage; excluding the lava pool produced by <a data-e=\"great-chaos-fire-orb\">Great Chaos Fire Orb<\/a>, this spell is the most powerful direct-damage pyromancy in the game. While both Great Chaos Fire Orb and <a data-e=\"seething-chaos\">Seething Chaos<\/a> can deal more damage under optimal circumstances, enemies can move away from the lava pool left by Great Chaos Fire Orb, and Seething Chaos requires manipulation and timing in order to deal the most damage.<\/p><p>Unlike its predecessor, Chaos Bed Vestiges does not leave a lava pool, has less range and will begin to arc after a shorter distance (approximately slightly longer than <a data-e=\"fire-orb\">Fire Orb<\/a>). However, it is easier to reach enemies at higher elevations with this spell than it is with the various &quot;fireball&quot; spells. As well, like its predecessor, its extremely short cast time and fast travel speed allows players to use this spell to quickly punish enemies' openings. <br><br><\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-the-old-demon-king","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Chaos_Bed_Vestiges"},{"id":"chaos-storm","kind":"spell","name":"Chaos Storm","page":"Chaos Storm (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Chaos_Storm__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":2,"fp":"3","req":{"int":0,"fth":0},"buy":12000,"desc":"Art of the Flame of Chaos, from Ancient Izalith. Erects multiple chaos fire pillars in vicinity.\nChaotic flame melts even great boulders, and creates a brief surge of molten lava on impact.\nThe all-engulfing Chaos Flame eventually formed a tumultuous seedbed, which birthed the twisted things known as Demons.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 12,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"izalith-pyromancy-tome\">Izalith Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster focuses power in the catalyst, and then lays down a sweeping wide blanket of erupting fire pillars. Each pillar will inflict 1.95 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage and knock any targets skyward. After eruption, a lava pool will persist at the eruption point, inflicting 0.9 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage to any enemy that touches it.<\/p><p>The FP cost of this spell is expressed per-pillar. Upon initial successful cast, the spell will consume 13 FP (11 FP with the <a data-e=\"dusk-crown-ring\">Dusk Crown Ring<\/a> equipped), and additional Focus is consumed as each pillar materializes. A maximum of 15 pillars (including the one created by the initial cast) can be conjured in a single cast of this spell, resulting in total consumption of 55 FP (53 FP with Dusk Crown Ring equipped). <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Chaos_Storm_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"crystal-hail","kind":"spell","name":"Crystal Hail","page":"Crystal Hail","img":"assets/img/Crystal_Hail.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"19","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":1500,"desc":"Unique sorcery developed by extraordinary preacher twins known as the Crystal Sages.\nCasts a cascade of small crystal soulmasses from above. Crystal soulmasses have piercing qualities.\nIn a pact said to have been formed long ago, one of the Sages allied with the Undead Legion in order to train the sorcerers of Farron.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-a-crystal-sage\">Soul of a Crystal Sage<\/a> and 1,500 souls with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a large crystal mass, which rises skyward. After a short delay, the crystal mass sequentially launches numerous crystal soulmasses, 22 in total, which rain down on the general area. Each soulmass has minor tracking capability, homing in on targets within the area and inflicting 0.62 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage upon impact, as well as minor stagger. <br><br><\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-a-crystal-sage","cost":"1,500 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Crystal_Hail"},{"id":"crystal-magic-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Crystal Magic Weapon","page":"Crystal Magic Weapon (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Crystal_Magic_Weapon__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"45","req":{"int":30,"fth":null},"buy":10000,"desc":"Further sharpens Magic Weapon via crystallization.\nReinforces right weapon with crystal.\nAfter much experimentation, Logan found the crystal medium facilitated a strong bond between weapon and soul.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 10,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"crystal-scroll\">Crystal Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces right-hand weapon with Magic, adding 95% of the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage for 60 seconds. The duration of the buff can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>For catalysts that scale with both Intelligence and Faith, only the Intelligence portion of the Spell Buff is counted. Special catalysts such as the <a data-e=\"archdeacons-great-staff\">Archdeacon's Great Staff<\/a> and <a data-e=\"man-grubs-staff\">Man-grub's Staff<\/a> are treated as having the base 100 Spell Buff.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Crystal_Magic_Weapon_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"crystal-soul-spear","kind":"spell","name":"Crystal Soul Spear","page":"Crystal Soul Spear (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Crystal_Soul_Spear__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"46","req":{"int":48,"fth":null},"buy":15000,"desc":"Further sharpens Soul Spear via crystallization.\nFires a piercing crystal soul spear.\nAccording to the Crystal Sages, old Big Hat achieved enlightment within the Regal Archives, where he came to find the quintessence of sorcery in the facets of a certain crystal.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 15,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"crystal-scroll\">Crystal Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>An enhanced version of <a data-e=\"soul-spear\">Soul Spear<\/a>, and one of the most devastating Sorceries in the game. Fires a piercing crystal soul spear that can go through a line of enemies, inflicting 3.05 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage upon any enemies struck. The spear has long range and fast travel speed, but requires a longer cast time.<\/p><p>Alongside Soul Spear, this spell has the longest range among all Sorceries.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Crystal_Soul_Spear_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"dark-blade","kind":"spell","name":"Dark Blade","page":"Dark Blade","img":"assets/img/Dark_Blade.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"35","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":10000,"desc":"Miracle of the Sable Church of Londor.\nReinforces weapons with dark.\nThe third daughter Liliane, one of the founders of the Sable Church, is said to recount tales that portray the suffering and conflict of Hollows.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 10,000 souls once either of them has been given the <a data-e=\"londor-braille-divine-tome\">Londor Braille Divine Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces right hand weapon with Dark damage. It adds 85% of an equipped talisman/sacred chime's Spell Buff as Dark damage for the next 60 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Blade"},{"id":"dark-edge","kind":"spell","name":"Dark Edge","page":"Dark Edge","img":"assets/img/Dark_Edge.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"26","req":{"int":30,"fth":null},"buy":8000,"desc":"A forbidden dark sorcery. Strikes with blade formed of humanity's darkness.\nPassed from mother to daughter, this blade was intended for both protection and as a means of taking one's own life. The young girl never swung it more than once.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 8,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a blade imbued with Dark energy, striking down vertically in front of the player. The blade will inflict 2.05 times the Spell Buff of the wielded catalyst as Dark Damage, which can be boosted by wielding a dark catalyst. The sword can hit targets through walls, as well as foes above the wielder.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Edge"},{"id":"darkmoon-blade","kind":"spell","name":"Darkmoon Blade","page":"Darkmoon Blade (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Darkmoon_Blade__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"50","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle of those who devoted themselves to the Darkmoon covenant.\nReinforces right weapon with Darkmoon light.\nMiracles of the Darkmoon are tales of revenge, but Captain Yorshka recites only for the sake of remembering her brother, without knowledge of its meaning.\nPerhaps this is better, as revenge is better left to the Blades.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 2 in the <a data-e=\"blade-of-the-darkmoon\">Blade of the Darkmoon<\/a> covenant. To achieve this, the player must offer 30 <a data-e=\"proof-of-a-concord-kept\">Proofs of a Concord Kept<\/a> to <a data-e=\"company-captain-yorshka\">Company Captain Yorshka<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces the player's right hand weapon with Darkmoon light, adding 95% of casting talisman/sacred chime's Spell Buff as Magic damage for the next 60 seconds.<\/p><p><a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a> increases the duration to 78 seconds.<\/p><p>For catalysts that scale with both Intelligence and Faith, such as <a data-e=\"caithas-chime\">Caitha's Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"white-hair-talisman\">White Hair Talisman<\/a>, only the Faith portion of the Spell Buff is accounted for.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Darkmoon_Blade_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"dead-again","kind":"spell","name":"Dead Again","page":"Dead Again (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Dead_Again__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"45","req":{"int":15,"fth":23},"buy":5000,"desc":"Sacrilegious miracle of the Sable Church of Londor\nBless corpses, transforming them into traps.\nLondor, the Hollow Realm, is a society of undead, comprised of the corpses and shades of those who led unsavory lives. Is such blessing really something one must ponder?","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 5,000 souls once either of them has been given the <a data-e=\"londor-braille-divine-tome\">Londor Braille Divine Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon cast, a droplet of energy is released from the catalyst and lands on the ground. This will bless the three closest corpses to the caster, within a moderate radius. These corpses will explode after a brief delay, inflicting Dark damage to any nearby foes. The explosions can hit multiple foes.<\/p><p>The damage dealt by each explosion is a flat amount determined solely by the caster's Faith. It is not affected by wielding a catalyst that boosts the power of Dark Spells, such as the <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, nor is it affected by spell boosting equipment or Spell Buff (and therefore the upgrade level of the catalyst or increases from <a data-e=\"ring-of-the-suns-first-born\">Ring of the Sun's First Born<\/a> or Awakening). However, each explosion's damage output can be increased by secondary pieces of equipment that affect Dark damage, such as the Blindfold Mask, <a data-e=\"dark-clutch-ring\">Dark Clutch Ring<\/a> and <a data-e=\"red-tearstone-ring\">Red Tearstone Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>The damage for each explosion is expressed as follows:<\/p><table><tr><th>Faith<\/th><th>Damage<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>23-29<\/td><td>350<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>30-39<\/td><td>450<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>40-49<\/td><td>550<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>50-59<\/td><td>650<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>60-69<\/td><td>710<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>70-79<\/td><td>770<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>80-99<\/td><td>830<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dead_Again_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"deep-protection","kind":"spell","name":"Deep Protection","page":"Deep Protection","img":"assets/img/Deep_Protection.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":null,"fth":20},"buy":4000,"desc":"Miracle taught to inaugurated deacons of the Cathedral of the Deep\nSlightly boosts attack, damage absorption, and resistance, while also increasing stamina and recovery speed.\nThe deep was originally a peaceful and sacred place, but became the final rest for many abhorrent things. This tale of the Deep offers protection for those who worship amidst those horrors.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 4,000 souls once either of them has been given the <a data-e=\"deep-braille-divine-tome\">Deep Braille Divine Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases damage absorption across the board by 5%, status effect resistance by 20 in all categories, damage dealt by all weapons and spells by 5%, and stamina regeneration by 3 points per second. Buff lasts for 60 seconds.<\/p><p>In PvP, increases damage absorption by 2% and damage dealt by 2%.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deep_Protection"},{"id":"deep-soul","kind":"spell","name":"Deep Soul","page":"Deep Soul","img":"assets/img/Deep_Soul.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"6","req":{"int":12,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Sorcery of Archdeacon Royce and his deacons, said to have been imparted to them by McDonnell of the Boreal Valley.\nFires dark soul dregs.\nSouls which swell from the deep pursue their target, drawn towards life.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-deacons-of-the-deep\">Soul of the Deacons of the Deep<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a>. No souls are required to complete the transposition.<\/p>","use":"<p>Quickly conjures soul dregs, which slowly home in on the target, dealing 1.0 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage upon impact. Costs very little FP and stamina, and is subject to modification by Faith and Dark bonus on certain specialized catalysts.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-the-deacons-of-the-deep","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Deep_Soul"},{"id":"divine-pillars-of-light","kind":"spell","name":"Divine Pillars of Light","page":"Divine Pillars of Light","img":"assets/img/Divine_Pillars_of_Light.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"3","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle of Gertrude, the Heavenly Daughter.\nBrings down multiple pillars of light in the vicinity.\nThe Queen's holy maiden Gertrude was visited by an angel, who revealed this tale to her.\nDespite losing both her sight and her voice, she was determined to record the tale. Ordinary men cannot decipher her fragmentary scrawl, nor comprehend how it became the foundation of the Angelic faith of Lothric.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>, on Gertrude's lifeless body lying inside a large bird cage at the top of the archives. To reach it, enter the tower guarded by the three Gertrude's Knights and drop through the open hatch inside. Make way through the rafters and drop through the open door on top of the cage.<\/p>","use":"<p>When cast, multiple pillars of light will erupt at random points around the caster over a period of several seconds, each dealing 1.9 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as physical damage and knocking most opponents into the air. Each pillar is regarded as its own separate damage instance, meaning that getting hit by a pillar early in the cast will not prevent an enemy from being hit by another one in the same cast instance.<\/p><p>FP cost is based on the number of pillars summoned. Upon initial cast, 13 FP is consumed, and additional FP for each pillar afterward. A maximum of 15 pillars (including the one from the initial cast) can be called down for a total cost of 55 FP. Interrupting the caster will also halt the FP consumption of the Miracle.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Divine_Pillars_of_Light"},{"id":"dorhys-gnawing","kind":"spell","name":"Dorhys' Gnawing","page":"Dorhys' Gnawing","img":"assets/img/Dorhys__Gnawing.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle of Dorhys the deranged evangelist.\nSummons great insect swarm to feast on foes.\nThose who linger too long on the brink of the Deep will often slip. Dorhys is sure to have wallowed in this darkness, intoxicated by its peril.","avail":"<p>Guaranteed drop from the Evangelist in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Central Irithyll<\/a> bonfire, players must make their way past the plaza guarded by Irithyllian Slaves and Fire Witches. After veering to the left past the second Fire Witch and the pair of Pontiff Knights, a small terrace with a Crystal Lizard can be found. The banister closest to the building on the right-hand side is illusory, and will reveal a staircase once hit.<\/p><p>Heading down these stairs will bring the player to a smaller terrace guarded by another Pontiff Knight, and taking the next set of stairs leads to a ledge overlooking a courtyard. The Evangelist can be fought upon dropping down into this area, though she can also be fought from the ledge itself with magic or archery. The spell is awarded as soon as she is defeated.<\/p>","use":"<p>A stronger variant of <a data-e=\"gnaw\">Gnaw<\/a>. Fires a swarm of insects at the target, inflicting 1.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage and dealing 210 Bleed build-up. As a Dark Miracle, it is subject to augmentation from being cast using a Dark catalyst like <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>.<\/p><p>&lt;tabber&gt;Official translation= Miracle of Dorhys the deranged evangelist.<\/p><p>Summons great insect swarm to feast on foes.<\/p><p>Those who linger too long on the brink of the Deep will often slip. Dorhys is sure to have wallowed in this darkness, intoxicated by its peril. |-|Original description (Japanese) = 狂った教導師、ドーリスの奇跡<\/p><p>蟲の大群を召喚し、敵を酷く蝕む<\/p><p>深みの縁に立つ者は、ときに足を滑らせる 彼女は肥え、きっと酔ってもいたのだろう |-|Literal translation = Miracle of Doris, the mad preacher.<\/p><p>Summons a swarm of insects that severely devour the enemy.<\/p><p>Those who stand at the edge of the Deep sometimes slip to the bottom. She was fattened and must have been intoxicated. &lt;/tabber&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Dorhys'_Gnawing"},{"id":"emit-force","kind":"spell","name":"Emit Force","page":"Emit Force (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Emit_Force__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":null,"fth":18},"buy":null,"desc":"Traditional miracle of Catarina.\nReleases a shockwave in front.\nThe people of lands known for festivity and drink are typically outspoken. One can be sure that they will not bottle their emotions, instead venting anger and the like with confidence.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a gift from <a data-e=\"siegward-of-catarina\">Siegward of Catarina<\/a> by exhausting his dialogue in the kitchen found after the sewer area in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster briefly charges an orb, and then launches it forward. The orb will explode upon impact, inflicting 1.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as physical damage with direct contact, and stagger or knock down enemies caught in the explosion. The explosion inflicts 0.6 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst.<\/p><p>The orb has a long travel distance and does not arc, allowing the caster to knock down targets from very far away.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Emit_Force_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"farron-dart","kind":"spell","name":"Farron Dart","page":"Farron Dart","img":"assets/img/Farron_Dart.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"3","req":{"int":8,"fth":null},"buy":"Varies","desc":"Variation of Soul Arrow developed by sorcerers of the Undead Legion of Farron.\nFire a soul dart.\nWell known among the Farron sorceries, it is learned far and wide due to its ease of use.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> and <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 500 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>A miniaturized version of <a data-e=\"soul-arrow\">Soul Arrow<\/a>. Fires a soul dart at the target, dealing 0.52 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. The dart deals little damage and cannot inflict stagger on their targets, but cost very little FP and cast extremely quickly.<\/p><p>Unlike other Soul Arrow variants, Farron Dart can be cast while rolling and running. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Farron_Dart"},{"id":"farron-flashsword","kind":"spell","name":"Farron Flashsword","page":"Farron Flashsword","img":"assets/img/Farron_Flashsword.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"4","req":{"int":23,"fth":null},"buy":5000,"desc":"Alteration of Soul Greatsword developed by sorcerers of the Undead Legion of Farron.\nThe legion has a tendency to emphasize speed over power, and this practical alteration of an existing sorcery is no exception.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 5,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a sword made of souls from the staff and swings it quickly, dealing 1.03 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Magic damage to any enemy struck by the blade.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Farron_Flashsword"},{"id":"farron-hail","kind":"spell","name":"Farron Hail","page":"Farron Hail","img":"assets/img/Farron_Hail.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"4","req":{"int":28,"fth":null},"buy":5000,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Farron Dart. Fires a cascade of soul darts.\nEntrusted to the leader of the Legion's acolytes, and apparently a sorcery of his daughter, Heysel, that was refined by a Crystal Sage.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 5,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"sages-scroll\">Sage's Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster charges the catalyst for a short period, and then unleashes a barrage of soul darts in a spread in front of the caster, in four waves of five darts each (for a maximum of 20 total darts). Each wave inflicts 0.58 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage to any targets hit. It does not matter how many darts hit a target in each wave, the damage from a wave that strikes a target is always the same.<\/p><p>The FP cost is expressed as a per-wave basis, with a potential cost of 16 FP for all four waves (12 FP with <a data-e=\"dusk-crown-ring\">Dusk Crown Ring<\/a> equipped). Should the caster have enough FP for one wave but not all four, all waves will be cast regardless. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Farron_Hail"},{"id":"fire-orb","kind":"spell","name":"Fire Orb","page":"Fire Orb (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fire_Orb__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"14","req":{"int":8,"fth":8},"buy":3000,"desc":"The signature flame-manipulating spell common to pyromancers. Hurls a giant fire orb.\nThe blazing fire orb explodes on impact, dealing fire damage to the surrounding area.\nThey say that once a pyromancer learns this spell, their understanding of the flame deepens, together with a yearning for it.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 3,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome\">Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Hurls a fire orb at the target, inflicting 2.25 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. If the target is only caught in the splash of the explosion, they will take 2.1 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage.<\/p><p>Due to peculiarities in scaling it doesn't benefit from the Faith scaling of a Pyromancy Flame unless a minimum level of Intelligence has been reached: starting at 22 Intelligence for a +0 Flame and gradually going down to 18 Intelligence for a +10 Flame.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Orb_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"fire-surge","kind":"spell","name":"Fire Surge","page":"Fire Surge (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fire_Surge__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"2","req":{"int":6,"fth":null},"buy":1000,"desc":"Pyromancy of Cornyx of the Great Swamp. Emits a constant stream of fire.\nCornyx is a venerable pyromancer of an older mold, said to have restored a number of spells lost to the past, amongst which this is the most well-known.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Emits a constant stream of fire, with each tick inflicting 0.67 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Surge_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"fire-whip","kind":"spell","name":"Fire Whip","page":"Fire Whip (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fire_Whip__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"2","req":{"int":13,"fth":8},"buy":10000,"desc":"Primal pyromancy taught by Quelana, daughter of the Witch of Izalith. Sweeps foes with a fire whip.\nThe caster manipulates the flames at will, making this an extremely difficult spell to use.\nPyromancy is at once the knowledge of controlling flame, and the knowledge that control is impossible.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 10,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"quelana-pyromancy-tome\">Quelana Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a sweeping flame at point-blank range and waves it back and forth. The whip inflicts 0.65 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage for each instance that hits an enemy.<\/p><p>The FP cost of the spell is expressed per-instance. The whip will lash for 17 to 19 instances, consuming FP as each instance materializes, resulting in a total consumption of 34 to 38 FP. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fire_Whip_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"fireball","kind":"spell","name":"Fireball","page":"Fireball (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Fireball__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"10","req":{"int":6,"fth":6},"buy":1000,"desc":"Elementary pyromancy that is often the first learned. Hurls a fireball.\nTo use pyromancies, equip a pyromancy flame and attune a pyromancy at a bonfire.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Pyromancer class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Hurls a fireball at the target, inflicting 1.7 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. If the target is only caught in the splash of the explosion, they will take 1.55 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage.<\/p><p>Due to peculiarities in scaling it doesn't benefit from the Faith scaling of a Pyromancy Flame unless a minimum level of Intelligence has been reached: starting at 22 Intelligence for a +0 Flame and gradually going down to 18 Intelligence for a +10 Flame.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Fireball_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"firestorm","kind":"spell","name":"Firestorm","page":"Firestorm (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Firestorm__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"2","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":15000,"desc":"Primal pyromancy taught by Quelana, a daughter of the Witch of Izalith.\nSurrounds the caster with multiple pillars of flame.\nThe raging storm is indiscriminate; such is the intrinsic horror of the flame.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 15,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"quelana-pyromancy-tome\">Quelana Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The caster focuses power in the catalyst, and then lays down a sweeping wide blanket of erupting fire pillars. Each pillar will inflict 1.75 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage and knock any targets skyward.<\/p><p>The FP cost of this spell is expressed per-pillar. Upon initial successful cast, the spell will consume 12 FP (10 FP with the <a data-e=\"dusk-crown-ring\">Dusk Crown Ring<\/a> equipped), and additional Focus is consumed as each pillar materializes. A maximum of 15 pillars (including the one created by the initial cast) can be conjured in a single cast of this spell, resulting in total maximum consumption of 40 FP (38 FP with Dusk Crown Ring equipped), assuming that the spell is not interrupted. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Firestorm_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"flame-fan","kind":"spell","name":"Flame Fan","page":"Flame Fan","img":"assets/img/Flame_Fan.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"9","req":{"int":15,"fth":15},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancy of Zoey, descendant of the desert pyromancers.\nUse repeatedly to brush the fan left and right.\nZoey possessed true beauty, as did all the desert pyromancers, but hers did not poison, and so she became the unassuming queen of the feeble ones.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Desert Pyromancer Zoey.<\/p>","use":"<p>Upon cast, the player manifests a fiery fan and swipes it at enemies at melee range, inflicting 1.55 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. It can be used continuously by repeating the cast, alternating sweeping direction until FP or stamina is exhausted.<\/p><p>It inflicts stagger on enemies, subjecting them to Instability damage if they take another hit while recoiling, either from a second swipe with the fan or any other damage source.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Flame_Fan"},{"id":"flash-sweat","kind":"spell","name":"Flash Sweat","page":"Flash Sweat (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Flash_Sweat__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":6,"fth":6},"buy":1500,"desc":"Unique pyromancy of the Great Swamp associated with Carmina.\nIntense sweating increases fire damage absorption.\nAn influential pyromancy that internalizes flame, likely forming the foundation for many subsequent spells.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 1,500 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases Fire damage absorption by 30%. Buff lasts for 30 seconds. Duration can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Flash_Sweat_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"floating-chaos","kind":"spell","name":"Floating Chaos","page":"Floating Chaos","img":"assets/img/Floating_Chaos.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":16,"fth":16},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancer Dunnel was fascinated by this ceremonial art employed by the clerics of the Smouldering Lake.\nSummons a fire-spitting chaos orb.\nChaos burns away in the blink of an eye, but was the primordial life born in the Bed of Chaos, and a grievous symbol of Izalith's sin.","avail":"<p>Dropped by Livid Pyromancer Dunnel in the <a data-e=\"painted-world-of-ariandel\">Painted World of Ariandel<\/a>, who invades the player in Crossbreed Priscilla's boss arena.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a fire orb, which begins to levitate at its casting point. After 2.5 seconds, the orb begins shooting projectiles at the enemy that the caster was locked on to upon cast, launching three shots before dispersing. It can also shoot at the nearest enemy, if no hostile was locked on to. Each projectile will inflict 0.85 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage.<\/p><p>Multiple instances of this spell can be active at once.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Floating_Chaos"},{"id":"force","kind":"spell","name":"Force","page":"Force (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Force__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"26","req":{"int":null,"fth":12},"buy":1000,"desc":"Elementary miracle among clerics.\nCreates a shockwave.\nWhile it inflicts no direct damage,\nthis miracle propels foes back, staggering them.\nCan also defend against incoming arrows.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Cleric class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 1,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-carim\">Braille Divine Tome of Carim<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Propels enemies back, staggering them. Inflicts no damage. Can be used to neutralize incoming arrows.<\/p><p>Affected foes will be knocked in the facing direction of the caster. Mechanically, it inflicts the knockdown via Poise damage, so it is possible to ignore the spell's effects with enough Hyper Armor or via Unfaltering Prayer cast from the <a data-e=\"sunlight-talisman\">Sunlight Talisman<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Force_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"frozen-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Frozen Weapon","page":"Frozen Weapon","img":"assets/img/Frozen_Weapon.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"One of the spells left behind by the young sorcerer Sulyvahn before leaving the Painted World. Imbues right-hand weapon with frost.\nSulyvahn was born and raised inside the painting yet had little use for his frigid homeland, since he had not yet experienced loss.","avail":"<p>Found amongst the Giant Flies in an egg-infested area near the Rope Bridge Cave, shortly past the Snowfield.<\/p>","use":"<p>Adds 48 Frost build-up to right-hand weapon. Buff lasts for 60 seconds, but cannot be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Frozen_Weapon"},{"id":"gnaw","kind":"spell","name":"Gnaw","page":"Gnaw","img":"assets/img/Gnaw.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":null,"fth":18},"buy":2000,"desc":"Dark miracle taught in the Cathedral of the Deep.\nSummons insect swarm to feast on foes.\nThese insects which lurk in the Deep have tiny jaws lined with fangs to tear open the skin and burrow into the flesh in the blink of an eye, causing intense bleeding.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 2,000 souls once either of them has been given the <a data-e=\"deep-braille-divine-tome\">Deep Braille Divine Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Fires a swarm of insects at the target, inflicting 0.9 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage and dealing 150 Bleed build-up. As a Dark Miracle, it is subject to augmentation from being cast using a Dark catalyst like <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>.<\/p><p>&lt;tabber&gt;Official translation= Dark miracle taught in the Cathedral of the Deep.<\/p><p>Summons insect swarm to feast on foes.<\/p><p>These insects which lurk in the Deep have tiny jaws lined with fangs to tear open the skin and burrow into the flesh in the blink of an eye, causing intense bleeding. |-|Original description (Japanese) = 深みの聖堂に伝わる暗い奇跡<\/p><p>蟲の群れを召喚し、敵を蝕む<\/p><p>深みに潜む蟲たちは、小さな顎に牙を持ち 瞬く間に皮膚を裂き、肉に潜り込む それは激しい出血を伴うという |-|Literal translation = Dark miracle told in the Church of the Deep.<\/p><p>Summons a swarm of insects to devour the enemy.<\/p><p>The insects that lurk in the Deep have small jaws with fangs that tear the skin and burrow into the flesh in the blink of an eye. It is said to be accompanied by severe bleeding. &lt;/tabber&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Gnaw"},{"id":"great-chaos-fire-orb","kind":"spell","name":"Great Chaos Fire Orb","page":"Great Chaos Fire Orb","img":"assets/img/Great_Chaos_Fire_Orb.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":2,"fp":"32","req":{"int":0,"fth":0},"buy":10000,"desc":"Art of the Flame of Chaos, from Ancient Izalith. Hurls a great chaos fire orb.\nChaotic flame melts even great boulders, and creates a brief surge of molten lava on impact.\nThe Witch of Izalith and her daughters birthed the Flame of Chaos, but it devoured them along with their home.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 10,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"izalith-pyromancy-tome\">Izalith Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Hurls a large Chaos-infused fire orb at the target; whether they are hit by the projectile itself or caught by the explosion on impact, targets will take 3.3 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. A pool of lava will persist at the impact point for 3 seconds, inflicting 1.5 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage for as long as any enemy makes contact with it.<\/p><p>Due to peculiarities in scaling it doesn't benefit from the Faith scaling of a Pyromancy Flame unless a minimum level of Intelligence has been reached: starting at 22 Intelligence for a +0 Flame and gradually going down to 18 Intelligence for a +10 Flame.<br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Chaos_Fire_Orb"},{"id":"great-combustion","kind":"spell","name":"Great Combustion","page":"Great Combustion (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Combustion__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"17","req":{"int":10,"fth":10},"buy":3000,"desc":"Pyromancy which improves upon Combustion. Creates a powerful, giant flame in hand.\nA very powerful, yet simple spell to use.\nPyromancy is to at once know fear and longing, the resultant power of which depends on both the caster's intelligence and faith.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 3,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a powerful explosion in front of the caster, inflicting 1.95 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. If foes catch the lingering flame after the initial explosion, they will take only 1.85 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Combustion_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-deep-soul","kind":"spell","name":"Great Deep Soul","page":"Great Deep Soul","img":"assets/img/Great_Deep_Soul.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"9","req":{"int":20,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Deep Soul. Fires powerful darkened soul dregs.\nArchdeacon McDonnell, a sorcerer himself, delighted in the cathedral's stagnating souls. For him, they represented the glorious bedrock of this world.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 1 in the <a data-e=\"aldrich-faithful\">Aldrich Faithful<\/a> covenant. To achieve this, the player must offer 10 <a data-e=\"human-dregs\">Human Dregs<\/a> to <a data-e=\"archdeacon-mcdonnell\">Archdeacon McDonnell<\/a> in the Water Reserve.<\/p>","use":"<p>Quickly fires powerful darkened soul dregs that home in on the target, inflicting 1.3 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage upon impact. Has a short cast time similar to <a data-e=\"deep-soul\">Deep Soul<\/a>, and can benefit from Faith scaling as well as Dark bonus depending on the catalyst used.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Deep_Soul"},{"id":"great-farron-dart","kind":"spell","name":"Great Farron Dart","page":"Great Farron Dart","img":"assets/img/Great_Farron_Dart.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"4","req":{"int":23,"fth":null},"buy":2000,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Farron Dart. Fires a more powerful soul dart.\nEntrusted to the leader of the Legion's acolytes, and apparently a sorcery of his daughter, Heysel, that was refined by a Crystal Sage.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 2,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"sages-scroll\">Sage's Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>An upscaled version of <a data-e=\"farron-dart\">Farron Dart<\/a>. Fires a powerful soul dart at the target, dealing 0.59 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. Like Farron Dart, it cannot stagger enemies hit by the projectiles but casts extremely quickly and costs little FP, and like Farron Dart it has special rolling and running attacks which make it extremely flexible.<\/p><p>The spell's larger damage multiplier compared to Farron Dart allows it to break through low values of Magic Defense more easily (such as against players that do not level Intelligence). As a result, it inflicts damage that increases roughly in tandem with its FP cost, meaning that it can still deal respectable damage without being as inefficient as the multiplier difference would suggest. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Farron_Dart"},{"id":"great-heal","kind":"spell","name":"Great Heal","page":"Great Heal (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Heal__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"65","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":null,"desc":"Glorious miracle used by high-ranking clerics. Restores a large amount of HP for self and those in the vicinity.\nOnly a select few have learned to recite the epic tale in its entirety, but those who do are amply rewarded.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-of-the-boreal-valley\">Irithyll of the Boreal Valley<\/a>.<\/p><p>Upon reaching the swamp area below the city, past the dark room filled with Irithyllian Slaves, follow the right side to find the corpse of a Man-grub holding the spell. It is guarded by two Sewer Centipedes.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores HP for the caster and nearby allies equal to 5.5 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, and consumes 205 stamina. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account.<\/p><p>Due to the high stamina cost of this spell, action after casting is severely restricted, preventing the caster from rolling or attacking immediately after. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Heal_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-heavy-soul-arrow","kind":"spell","name":"Great Heavy Soul Arrow","page":"Great Heavy Soul Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Heavy_Soul_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"14","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":4000,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Heavy Soul Arrow.\nFires a more powerful heavy soul arrow\nSorceries are a logical discipline; their strength influenced by the caster's intelligence.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 4,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for the same price once she has been given <a data-e=\"orbecks-ashes\">Orbeck's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The most powerful version of the basic <a data-e=\"soul-arrow\">Soul Arrow<\/a>, and an enhanced version of <a data-e=\"heavy-soul-arrow\">Heavy Soul Arrow<\/a>. Fires a heavy soul arrow, dealing 2.42 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. Has the same casting time as Heavy Soul Arrow, while dealing more damage.<\/p><p>As the large multiplier on a single damage instance allows it to easily break through low to moderate values of Magic defense on the target, reducing its effectiveness, Great Heavy Soul Arrow is the most efficient Sorcery in the game, in terms of damage-to-FP ratio, once reductions from defense and absorption are factored in. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Heavy_Soul_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-lightning-spear","kind":"spell","name":"Great Lightning Spear","page":"Great Lightning Spear (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Lightning_Spear__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"32","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":null,"desc":"Primal account of Lightning Spear, which tells of an ancestral dragonslayer.\nHurls a giant lightning spear.\nGwyn, the First Lord, slew dragons with his sunlight spear, a tradition upheld by his firstborn and the greatspear he wielded.\nMuch of this resplendent tale of father and son, while epic, remains tragically untold.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 2 in the <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Warrior of Sunlight<\/a> covenant. To achieve this, the player must offer 30 <a data-e=\"sunlight-medal\">Sunlight Medals<\/a> to the Sunlight Altar in <a data-e=\"lothric-castle\">Lothric Castle<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a large spear made of Lightning, then hurls it at the target. The projectile inflicts 1.85 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage.<\/p><p>When cast at extremely close range, the spear will inflict an additional 1.45 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage. A successful point-blank cast will also result in vibration feedback through the player's controller, providing confirmation of inflicting additional damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Lightning_Spear_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-magic-barrier","kind":"spell","name":"Great Magic Barrier","page":"Great Magic Barrier (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Magic_Barrier__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"40","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":null,"desc":"The tale which was later interpreted as Magic Barrier.\nGreatly increases the magic damage absorption by covering the body in a strong white protective coating.\nSaid to be a tale of Havel the Rock, arch enemy of Seath the Scaleless. Havel despised magic, and was never complacent in preparing means to counter it.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>. From the rooftop where Havel the Rock stands before a dead wyvern, hug the left and drop down into a hidden area below. Follow the path to where a Rock Lizard guards the miracle.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases Magic absorption by 60%. Buff lasts for 70 seconds.<\/p><p>Unlike most other buffs, this value is the same in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Magic_Barrier_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-magic-shield","kind":"spell","name":"Great Magic Shield","page":"Great Magic Shield","img":"assets/img/Great_Magic_Shield.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"60","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Magic Shield. Greatly reinforces left shield with magic.\nOnly sorcerer-swordsmen with special duties are permitted the use of this spell, which temporarily grants even the smallest of shields fortitude more akin to that of a greatshield.","avail":"<p>Dropped by a Corpse Grub in a cell found in the <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>. After the first Jailer, drop down one floor and open the door to the creature.<\/p>","use":"<p>Greatly reinforces shield in the left hand, increasing damage absorption in all categories to 100% regardless of prior resistances, while increasing stability by 50%. Skills that inflict damage through raised shields such as Blind Spot and Shield Splitter will also be completely blocked. Effects last for 30 seconds, and duration can be increased by equipping a <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Magic_Shield"},{"id":"great-magic-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Great Magic Weapon","page":"Great Magic Weapon (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Magic_Weapon__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"35","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Magic Weapon. Greatly reinforces right weapon with magic.\nOnly sorcerer-swordsmen with special duties are permitted use of this spell. The azure blade is said to cut down heavily armored knights with ease.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>, down the path from the Farron Keep Perimeter bonfire, past the Ravenous Crystal Lizard and near the shortcut gate back to the Crucifixion Woods.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces right-hand weapon with Magic, adding 85% of the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage for 60 seconds. The duration of the buff can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>For catalysts that scale with both Intelligence and Faith, only the Intelligence portion of the Spell Buff is counted. Special catalysts such as the <a data-e=\"archdeacons-great-staff\">Archdeacon's Great Staff<\/a> and <a data-e=\"man-grubs-staff\">Man-grub's Staff<\/a> are treated as having the base 100 Spell Buff. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Magic_Weapon_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-soul-arrow","kind":"spell","name":"Great Soul Arrow","page":"Great Soul Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Great_Soul_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"10","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":3000,"desc":"Sorcery which improves upon Soul Arrow. Fires a more powerful soul arrow.\nMany sorceries inflict magic damage, making them effective against iron armor, tough scales, and other physically resilient materials.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 3,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for the same price once she has been given <a data-e=\"orbecks-ashes\">Orbeck's Ashes<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>A stronger variant of <a data-e=\"soul-arrow\">Soul Arrow<\/a>. Fires a soul arrow at the target, dealing 1.5 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. Has the same cast time as Soul Arrow but deals more damage, though still less than <a data-e=\"heavy-soul-arrow\">Heavy Soul Arrow<\/a>. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Soul_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"great-soul-dregs","kind":"spell","name":"Great Soul Dregs","page":"Great Soul Dregs","img":"assets/img/Great_Soul_Dregs.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":40,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"A sorcery that fires great dark soul dregs that have stewed for ages, far within the deep.\nThis sorcery is the highest form of Deep Soul.\nSome of the murkmen who rise from the depths are possessed by soul dregs, which have a grave likeness to the human form.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>. After finding the first Lothric Knights in the area, players can exit to the left of the small chapel and into a building infested with Murkmen. At the end of the corridor is an illusory wall that reveals a staircase to the second floor. The spell can be found at the end of the last room, guarded by numerous Dregs-possessed Murkmen.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a large soul dreg which accelerates upon cast and homes in on its target, exploding and inflicting 2.55 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Dark damage upon impact. Certain Dark catalysts will boost the damage output of this spell, and allow the wielder to take advantage of Faith scaling.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Soul_Dregs"},{"id":"heal","kind":"spell","name":"Heal","page":"Heal (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Heal__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"45","req":{"int":null,"fth":12},"buy":1000,"desc":"Elementary miracle cast by clerics. Restores HP for self and those in the vicinity.\nTo use miracles, equip a talisman or sacred chime and attune a miracle at a bonfire.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting spell for Cleric class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Restores HP for the caster and nearby allies equal to 3 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, and consumes 92 stamina. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"heal-aid","kind":"spell","name":"Heal Aid","page":"Heal Aid","img":"assets/img/Heal_Aid.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"27","req":{"int":null,"fth":8},"buy":500,"desc":"Miracle imparted as charity to those of little faith.\nSlightly restores HP.\nTo use miracles, equip a talisman or sacred chime and attune a miracle at a bonfire.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting spell for Herald class.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 500 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Restores HP for the caster equal to 1.5 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, and consumes 61 stamina. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account.<\/p><p>Unlike other healing Miracles, this spell does not force the caster to kneel down in prayer, and casts extremely quickly. However, it only heals the user and not nearby allies, unlike the other healing Miracles. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Heal_Aid"},{"id":"heavy-soul-arrow","kind":"spell","name":"Heavy Soul Arrow","page":"Heavy Soul Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Heavy_Soul_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"11","req":{"int":13,"fth":null},"buy":2000,"desc":"Elementary, yet practical sorcery from long ago. Fires a heavy soul arrow.\nOffers greater power but slower casting time, entailing a vulnerability that makes this sorcery trickier to handle.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Sorcerer class.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> (or by <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> after his death) for 2,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for the same price.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>A heavy version of <a data-e=\"soul-arrow\">Soul Arrow<\/a>. Fires a heavy soul arrow, dealing 2.15 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. Inflicts more damage than Soul Arrow and <a data-e=\"great-soul-arrow\">Great Soul Arrow<\/a>, but has a moderate casting time. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Soul_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"hidden-body","kind":"spell","name":"Hidden Body","page":"Hidden Body (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Hidden_Body__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":3000,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden sorceries. Turns body nigh on invisible.\nAlthough perfect invisibility is unachievable due to the risk of dissipation, the caster need only stand still for a moment to blend in to environs with astounding camouflage.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 3,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Turns the caster nearly invisible for 15 seconds. This duration can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Body_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"hidden-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Hidden Weapon","page":"Hidden Weapon (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Hidden_Weapon__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":12,"fth":null},"buy":1500,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden sorceries. Turns right weapon invisible.\nThe weapon itself undergoes no inherent changes. Effective use of this, like any tool, perhaps, is reliant upon the ingenuity of its caster.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 1,500 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Turns the caster's right-hand weapon completely invisible. Buff lasts for 45 seconds, and can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>As it is technically a weapon buff, it can only be cast on weapons that are capable of being buffed. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Hidden_Weapon_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"homeward","kind":"spell","name":"Homeward","page":"Homeward (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Homeward__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":null,"fth":18},"buy":3000,"desc":"Miracle taught to traveling clerics. Returns caster to the last bonfire used for resting, or to the bonfire in the shrine.\nIt would normally link to one's homeland, only the curse of the Undead has twisted its power, redirecting casters to a bonfire. Perhaps for the Undead, the bonfire serves as home.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 3,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Casting this miracle will present the player with the option of teleporting to either <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> or to the last bonfire they rested at.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Homeward_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"homing-crystal-soulmass","kind":"spell","name":"Homing Crystal Soulmass","page":"Homing Crystal Soulmass (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Homing_Crystal_Soulmass__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"43","req":{"int":30,"fth":null},"buy":18000,"desc":"Sharpens Homing Soulmass via crystallization.\nReleases homing crystal soulmass. Crystal soulmass has piercing qualities.\nAccording to the Crystal Sages, old Big Hat achieved enlightment within the Regal Archives where he came to find the quintessence of sorcery in the facets of a certain crystal.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 18,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"crystal-scroll\">Crystal Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>An upgraded form of <a data-e=\"homing-soulmass\">Homing Soulmass<\/a>. Conjures a number of crystalline orbs above the caster, requiring a longer casting time than Homing Soulmass. These orbs will automatically target and fly at any enemy that gets close enough to the caster's frontal arc, with each orb dealing 0.65 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage upon collision, inflicting stagger upon impact.<\/p><p>If the crystal orbs collide with any solid level geometry without flying at a target, they will automatically explode. However, unlike Homing Soulmass, they will not self-destruct when they collide with destructible level geometry (e.g., chairs, tables), instead destroying them while remaining ready to trigger.<\/p><p>The number of orbs conjured is dependent on the caster's Intelligence:<\/p><table><tr><th>Intelligence<\/th><th>Number of Orbs<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>30<\/td><td>4<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>31-99<\/td><td>5<\/td><\/tr><\/table>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Homing_Crystal_Soulmass_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"homing-soulmass","kind":"spell","name":"Homing Soulmass","page":"Homing Soulmass (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Homing_Soulmass__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":20,"fth":null},"buy":6000,"desc":"Sorcery developed by Big Hat Logan, the great sorcerer who left the Dragon School in an age long past.\nReleases homing soulmass.\nThis sorcery may offer a clue as to what Logan sought, but further investigation suggests its attraction to living things mirrors the nature of the dark.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 6,000 souls once he has been given <a data-e=\"logans-scroll\">Logan's Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Quickly conjures up a number of floating orbs above the caster. Orbs will automatically target and fly at any enemy that gets close enough to the caster's frontal arc, with each orb inflicting 0.49 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage upon collision, staggering the target for each impact. If the orbs collide with any level geometry without flying at a target, they will automatically explode, destroying any destructible objects and then vanishing.<\/p><p>The number of orbs conjured is dependent on the caster's Intelligence:<\/p><table><tr><th>Intelligence<\/th><th>Number of Orbs<\/th><\/tr><tr><td>20-24<\/td><td>3<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>25-30<\/td><td>4<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>31-99<\/td><td>5<\/td><\/tr><\/table><p><br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Homing_Soulmass_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"iron-flesh","kind":"spell","name":"Iron Flesh","page":"Iron Flesh (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Iron_Flesh__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"40","req":{"int":8,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancy that internalizes flame.\nIron flesh boosts damage absorption and resistance, but significantly increases weight.\nNot advisable for walking in marshlands, perhaps resulting in its obsolescence in the Great Swamp.","avail":"<p>Found in the poisonous swamp in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>. From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a> bonfire, enter the swamp and turn right. The spell can be seen amongst some trees in the middle of the swamp, within the deep water leading to the Basilisks.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases physical absorption by 40%, while decreasing Lightning absorption by 60%, and increases all status effect resistances by 45. Also grants the player constant Hyper Armor for the duration of the spell, but in return greatly increases their weight to the point where only slow-walking and fat-rolling are possible.<\/p><p>Cast animation takes 2 seconds to complete, and spell effect is active for 17 seconds. Duration of the buff can be extended via equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Iron_Flesh_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lifehunt-scythe","kind":"spell","name":"Lifehunt Scythe","page":"Lifehunt Scythe (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Lifehunt_Scythe__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":null,"fth":22},"buy":5000,"desc":"Miracle of Aldrich, Devourer of Gods.\nSteals HP of foes using an illusory scythe.\nAldrich dreamt as he slowly devoured the God of the Darkmoon. In this dream, he perceived the form of a young, pale girl in hiding.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-aldrich\">Soul of Aldrich<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 5,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>When cast, a scythe will materialize in the caster's hands, which is then swiped in an arc in front of the caster. The scythe inflicts 2.05 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Dark damage, and is subject to modification by casting with a dark catalyst like the <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>.<\/p><p>Upon hit, this spell also restores HP on the caster, between 0.73 and 0.88 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, being more effective with higher Faith; if multiple targets are hit, the caster will be healed multiple times. Unlike its damage, however, the heal does not scale with Intelligence, making it less effective depending on the catalyst used.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-aldrich","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lifehunt_Scythe_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lightning-arrow","kind":"spell","name":"Lightning Arrow","page":"Lightning Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"19","req":{"int":null,"fth":35},"buy":null,"desc":"The few female knights who served in the age of the gods used this miracle for dragonslaying.\nDraw lightning bow to fire a lightning arrow.\nThe lightning arrows offer a great improvement to the range of the spears, and were said to have been used to pierce the eyes of the dragons from afar.\nBut remember, beautiful stories are always marked by embellishment.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-ringed-city\">The Ringed City<\/a>, after the Shared Grave bonfire.<\/p><p>In the building with the shortcut to the Ringed Inner Wall bonfire, in the lowest room, hit the wall to the right of the stairs to reveal an Illusory Wall containing a Hobbled Cleric. Past the cleric are two more Illusory Walls, beyond which this miracle can be found.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a bow and arrow made of Lightning and holds it ready.<\/p><p>Much like a regular bow and arrow, the projectile remains nocked while the cast button is held, and is fired upon its release; there is a delay before the arrow can be released, which is subject to casting speed. FP is only consumed upon launching the arrow, and the spell can be cancelled by rolling out at any time. When casting this Miracle with a Talisman, using the Unfaltering Prayer weapon art will allow the player to retain their Hyper Armor up until the projectile is released.<\/p><p>The arrow inflicts 1.6 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage. While it does not have the point-blank bonus modifier of the <a data-e=\"lightning-spear\">Lightning Spear<\/a> family of Miracles, Lightning Arrow has significantly more range and a higher travel speed, making it much harder to dodge. As well, it costs less FP than Lightning Spear, allowing the caster to use it more frequently before having to replenish their Focus Points.<\/p><p>&lt;tabber&gt;Official translation= The few female knights who served in the age of the gods used this miracle for dragonslaying.<\/p><p>Draw lightning bow to fire a lightning arrow.<\/p><p>The lightning arrows offer a great improvement to the range of the spears, and were said to have been used to pierce the eyes of the dragons from afar. But remember, beautiful stories are always marked by embellishment. |-|Original description (Japanese) = 神々の時代、数少ない女騎士たちが 竜狩りに用いた奇跡<\/p><p>雷の弓を引き絞り、雷の矢を射る<\/p><p>槍に比べて射程距離に優れ 彼方から竜の瞳を射抜いたともいう 美々しい物語には、誇張が付き物だ |-|Literal translation = Miracle used by the few female knights that hunt dragons in the Age of the Gods.<\/p><p>Draw the lightning bow and shoot a lightning arrow.<\/p><p>It has a greater range compared to a spear, and is said to have been able to pierce a dragon's eye from the distance. Beautiful stories are often full of exaggerations. &lt;/tabber&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lightning-blade","kind":"spell","name":"Lightning Blade","page":"Lightning Blade","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Blade.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"50","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle allegedly wielded by a certain dragonslayer knight in the Age of Gods.\nReinforces right weapon with lightning.\nTales of dragonslayers are now a rare thing, told only in fragments and whispers in remote regions.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>. Take the left-hand exit upon reaching the bottom floor of the dungeon patrolled by multiple Jailers, towards the statues praying towards <a data-e=\"archdragon-peak\">Archdragon Peak<\/a>, and find the elevator that leads back up to the upper cell blocks. Activate the elevator, then turn around and drop off it on the way up. The Miracle can be found on a corpse hidden in an alcove.<\/p>","use":"<p>Reinforces right-hand weapon with Lightning. Adds 95% of equipped talisman/sacred chime's Spell Buff as Lightning damage for 60 seconds.<\/p><p><a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a> increases the duration to 78 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Blade"},{"id":"lightning-spear","kind":"spell","name":"Lightning Spear","page":"Lightning Spear (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Spear__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"23","req":{"int":null,"fth":20},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle allegedly used by Warriors of Sunlight.\nHurls a lightning Spear.\nThe spears inflict lightning damage, providing an effective counter to magic or fire. Especially powerful against metal armor and dragons.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Farron Keep<\/a>.<\/p><p>From the <a data-e=\"farron-keep\">Old Wolf of Farron<\/a> bonfire, take the lift up and climb the stairs to the right. Turn towards the closed gate opposite the Stray Demon and search for a broken railing that can be dropped through onto several ledges that lead beyond the gate. The miracle can be found in an open area amongst two Crystal Lizards, near a dead wyvern.<\/p>","use":"<p>Conjures a spear made of Lightning, then hurls it at the target. The projectile inflicts 1.45 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage.<\/p><p>When cast at extremely close range, the spear will inflict an additional 1.15 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage. A successful point-blank cast will also result in vibration feedback through the player's controller, providing confirmation of inflicting additional damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Spear_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"lightning-stake","kind":"spell","name":"Lightning Stake","page":"Lightning Stake","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Stake.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"34","req":{"int":null,"fth":35},"buy":null,"desc":"A lost dragonslaying miracle.\nStrikes with a stake of lightning.\nThis tale describes the lost practices of ancient dragonslayers, who found that in order to pierce dragonscale, lightning should not be hurled as a bolt, but rather be thrust as a stake directly into the dragon's hide, to be truly effective.","avail":"<p>Dropped by the Carthus Sand Worm in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a large stake made of Lightning, and then plunges it into the ground. The spell has a very short range, but inflicts damage in an area around the impact point.<\/p><p>The stake can inflict up to four instances of damage, depending on how long any valid targets are standing within the impact radius. In quick succession, the stake will deal 0.9, 1.45, 1.45 and 0.8 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage to any enemies that are immediately in front of the caster. While short-ranged, the combined total damage will exceed that dealt by <a data-e=\"great-lightning-spear\">Great Lightning Spear<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Stake"},{"id":"lightning-storm","kind":"spell","name":"Lightning Storm","page":"Lightning Storm","img":"assets/img/Lightning_Storm.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"36","req":{"int":null,"fth":45},"buy":5000,"desc":"Miracle of the Nameless King, ally to the ancient dragons.\nCalls forth furious bolts of lightning.\nOnce a slayer of dragons, the former king and wargod tamed a Stormdrake, on which he led a lifetime of battle. This miracle is likely a tale of their bond.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-nameless-king\">Soul of the Nameless King<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 5,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster charges the catalyst for a short period of time, then releases power, creating numerous arcs of Lightning at the caster's feet that radiate outward. The shockwave from the cast, as well as each individual Lightning arc, will inflict 1.3 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage and 166 Fire damage.<\/p><p>Each individual arc is capable of inflicting repeated instances of damage to any enemy that stands within its immediate area, allowing this spell to hit the same target numerous times, being more damaging the closer they are standing to the caster. The concentrated nature of the Lightning arcs makes this spell extremely difficult if outright impossible to roll through, meaning that the only way to avoid damage is to stand far away from the caster.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-the-nameless-king","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Lightning_Storm"},{"id":"magic-barrier","kind":"spell","name":"Magic Barrier","page":"Magic Barrier (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Magic_Barrier__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":5000,"desc":"Miracle of clerics who wield weapons.\nIncreases magic damage absorption by covering the body in a white protective coating.\nThere was a short period in history where clerics and sorcerers opposed one another. Thus it became necessary for even simple clerics to have some means of opposing magic.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 5,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-lothric\">Braille Divine Tome of Lothric<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases Magic absorption by 35%. Buff lasts for 90 seconds, or 1 minute and 30 seconds.<\/p><p>Unlike most other buffs, this value is the same in PvP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Barrier_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"magic-shield","kind":"spell","name":"Magic Shield","page":"Magic Shield (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Magic_Shield__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":10,"fth":null},"buy":"Varies","desc":"Sorcery for casters who wield swords. Reinforces left shield with magic.\nShields augmented by magic have higher stability and damage absorption.\nEven the smallest of shields can be toughened considerably with the use of this spell.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> (or <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> after his death) for 4,500 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 3,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Reinforces the player's left-hand shield. Increases damage absorption while increasing stability by 20%.<\/p><p>Percentage of damage that chips through a raised shield is reduced by 30%, so weaker shields get larger absorption bonuses. For example, if a shield would normally block 50% of Fire damage, buffing it with Magic Shield would allow it to block 65%; if a shield blocks 80% of Fire damage, buffing it will cause it to block 86% of Fire damage. Therefore, chip damage can never be fully negated except in cases where absorption was already at 100% (e.g., physical damage).<\/p><p>Effect lasts for 60 seconds. Duration can be increased via equipping a <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>. Switching the weapon equipped in the off-hand away from the shield will remove the effect. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Shield_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"magic-weapon","kind":"spell","name":"Magic Weapon","page":"Magic Weapon (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Magic_Weapon__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":10,"fth":null},"buy":"Varies","desc":"Sorcery for casters who wield swords.\nReinforces right weapon with magic.\nThe power of the sorcerer-swordsmen of Vinheim is predicated upon this and Magic Shield Many warriors learnt sorcery just for this enchantment.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> (or <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> after his death) for 4,500 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 3,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Reinforces right-hand weapon with Magic, adding 75% of the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage for 90 seconds. This duration can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>For catalysts that scale with both Intelligence and Faith, only the Intelligence portion of the Spell Buff is counted. Special catalysts such as the <a data-e=\"archdeacons-great-staff\">Archdeacon's Great Staff<\/a> and <a data-e=\"man-grubs-staff\">Man-grub's Staff<\/a> are treated as having the base 100 Spell Buff. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Magic_Weapon_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"med-heal","kind":"spell","name":"Med Heal","page":"Med Heal (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Med_Heal__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"55","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":3500,"desc":"Miracle superior to Heal.\nRestores moderate HP for self and those in the vicinity.\nMiracles are fruit of the study of divine tales, a blessing received from the gods, through acts of prayer. Miracle strength depends on the caster's faith.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 3,500 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-carim\">Braille Divine Tome of Carim<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Restores HP for the caster and nearby allies equal to 4.1 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, and consumes 123 stamina. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account.<\/p><p>This is the highest tier instant-heal Miracle that does not completely deplete the stamina bar of the caster upon completion. Thus, it allows for action immediately after the spell ends, such as rolling to evade incoming danger. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Med_Heal_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"old-moonlight","kind":"spell","name":"Old Moonlight","page":"Old Moonlight","img":"assets/img/Old_Moonlight.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"23","req":{"int":25,"fth":null},"buy":15000,"desc":"A memory of an old sword found deep within Midir.\nThis sorcery uses souls to grant form to the thought, and attack with it.\nAttacks are coupled with lightwaves, and sustaining the stance before attacking increases their speed and potency.\nThe sword is named after moonlight, but it is slightly different than the one fashioned of the paledrake Seath. Perhaps it is rooted in an older memory, from not long after the Beginning.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-darkeater-midir\">Soul of Darkeater Midir<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 15,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a Moonlight Sword with the staff and holds it ready. It can be released at any time, performing a crosswise horizontal slash like <a data-e=\"soul-greatsword\">Soul Greatsword<\/a> while also unleashing a moonlight wave like the <a data-e=\"moonlight-greatsword\">Moonlight Greatsword<\/a>. FP is only consumed upon releasing the attack, and the caster can move slowly with the sword at the ready or roll to cancel it. The spell is made up of two components, the Moonlight Sword and the moonlight wave; the Moonlight Sword inflicts 1.25 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Magic damage, while the moonlight wave deals 1.5 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Magic damage.<\/p><p>If the spell is held for 2 seconds, the sword is charged with moonlight, increasing the damage dealt by the wave by 57%, causing it to inflict 2.35 times the Spell Buff of the wielded catalyst as Magic damage. The damage dealt by the sword itself is not affected by charging it. A charged beam deals damage comparable to <a data-e=\"great-heavy-soul-arrow\">Great Heavy Soul Arrow<\/a>, and will out-damage even <a data-e=\"crystal-soul-spear\">Crystal Soul Spear<\/a> if both the sword and the charged beam connect on the same target.<\/p><p>&lt;tabber&gt;Official translation= A memory of an old sword found deep within Midir. This sorcery uses souls to grant form to the thought, and attack with it.<\/p><p>Attacks are coupled with lightwaves, and sustaining the stance before attacking increases their speed and potency.<\/p><p>The sword is named after moonlight, but it is slightly different than the one fashioned of the paledrake Seath. Perhaps it is rooted in an older memory, from not long after the Beginning. |-|Original description (Japanese) = ミディールの深層にあった古い剣の記憶 それをソウルにより形作り、攻撃する魔術<\/p><p>攻撃は光波を伴い 攻撃前の構えを継続することで その威力、速度が増す<\/p><p>古い剣の名は、これもまた月光であるが 白竜シースのそれとは、少し姿が異なる その記憶は、よりはじまりに近いようだ |-|Literal translation = Memory of an old sword that existed deep within Midir. Sorcery that grants it form using the soul to attack with it.<\/p><p>Attack are accompanied by light waves, and by continuing to maintain the stance before the attack, its power and speed increase.<\/p><p>The name of the old sword is also Moonlight, but its appearance is slightly different from that of White Dragon Seath. That memory seems to be closer to the Beginning. &lt;/tabber&gt;<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Old_Moonlight"},{"id":"pestilent-mist","kind":"spell","name":"Pestilent Mist","page":"Pestilent Mist","img":"assets/img/Pestilent_Mist.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"13","req":{"int":30,"fth":null},"buy":1000,"desc":"Highly dangerous sorcery employed by Dragon School spooks. Only taught to trusted members.\nReleases dense mist that eats away at HP. Beware, as the caster is not immune to its effect.\nA body caught in the silent mist cloud lies still, while the face twists in a tortured scream. The names of these learned sorcerers became feared for this gruesome spectacle.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 1,000 souls once he has been given any Sorcery scroll.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a cloud of mist that deals damage to anything within it, including the caster. Mist persists for roughly 16.3 seconds, and deals damage at 5 instances per second for a total of 79 or 80 total instances of damage. The duration cannot be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p><p>The damage inflicted by Pestilent Mist, per instance, is calculated as follows:<\/p><p><i>10 + <\/i><\/p><p>Where <i>X<\/i> is the maximum HP of the target, rounded down to the nearest 1,000.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Pestilent_Mist"},{"id":"poison-mist","kind":"spell","name":"Poison Mist","page":"Poison Mist (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Poison_Mist__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"18","req":{"int":null,"fth":10},"buy":2000,"desc":"Unique pyromancy crafted by Eingyi, a heretic inhabiting the Great Swamp long ago. Creates a poison mist.\nEingyi was driven from the Great Swamp, however his pyromancy continues to succeed him.\nPerhaps dwellers of the Great Swamp were reminded that their very existence is one rooted in heresy.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 2,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome\">Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster reels back and then exhales a cloud of purple mist, inflicting 15 Poison buildup per tick to foes that stand in it. The cloud persists for 6 seconds.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Poison_Mist_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"power-within","kind":"spell","name":"Power Within","page":"Power Within (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Power_Within__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":10,"fth":10},"buy":null,"desc":"Forbidden pyromancy amongst those who internalize flame.\nTemporarily boost attack, but gradually lose HP.\nA pyromancer fears the flame.\nHowever, this fear subsides once it is accepted as a substitute for strength.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>. Inside the darkened room located after the big wax vat area, the first wax vat, look for a lever on a pillar along the wall between 2 bookcases and pull it. While facing the lever, a bookcase on your left will move, revealing a secret room with a corpse holding the spell.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases all damage dealt by the caster by 20%, as well as increasing stamina recovery speed by 30 points per second. The caster constantly loses approximately 1% of their maximum HP per second for the duration of the spell. Buff lasts for 30 seconds and does not stack with <a data-e=\"carthus-beacon\">Carthus Beacon<\/a>.<\/p><p>In PvP, attack power is increased by 15% instead.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Within_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"profaned-flame","kind":"spell","name":"Profaned Flame","page":"Profaned Flame","img":"assets/img/Profaned_Flame.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":25,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancy deriving from the Profaned Flame.\nEngulfs foes at range and burns them to ashes.\nThe Profaned Capital was consumed by fire after Yhorm the Giant became a Lord of Cinder. The fire, born of the sky, is said to have incinerated naught but human flesh.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"irithyll-dungeon\">Irithyll Dungeon<\/a>, on  the floor in the Giant Slave's cell. It is guarded by the giant itself and numerous Hound Rats.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster waves the catalyst, conjuring a flame at the target's location. The flames concentrate and focus at the location for approximately 1 second before exploding, inficting 2.6 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. The explosion will also knock down any enemies in the area.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Profaned_Flame"},{"id":"profuse-sweat","kind":"spell","name":"Profuse Sweat","page":"Profuse Sweat","img":"assets/img/Profuse_Sweat.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":6,"fth":6},"buy":2000,"desc":"Advanced pyromancy that internalizes flame, associated with Carmina.\nProfuse sweating temporarily boosts resistance to bleeding, poison, frost and curses.\nThe yellowish sweat cures all kinds of ailments.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"cornyx-of-the-great-swamp\">Cornyx of the Great Swamp<\/a> for 2,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"great-swamp-pyromancy-tome\">Great Swamp Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Temporarily increases resistance to Bleed, Poison, Frost and Curse buildup by 80. Buff lasts for 60 seconds, and can be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Profuse_Sweat"},{"id":"projected-heal","kind":"spell","name":"Projected Heal","page":"Projected Heal","img":"assets/img/Projected_Heal.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"55","req":{"int":null,"fth":28},"buy":null,"desc":"A miracle discovered in the last days of Lothric. Toss a light that heals those near the point of impact.\nEven those who had forgotten the caress and bounty of the Princess of Sunlight did their best to recall her image. The stories spun about her were most certainly childish, and yet gravely sincere.","avail":"<p>Found in <a data-e=\"the-dreg-heap\">The Dreg Heap<\/a>. After meeting <a data-e=\"amnesiac-lapp\">Amnesiac Lapp<\/a> for the first time, progress through the area past him guarded by numerous Murkmen. Upon reaching the area overlooking the Harald Legion Knight, look to the right, where there is an ash pile at the bottom of a drop leading to a battlement remnant being patrolled by a <a data-e=\"lothric-war-banner\">banner<\/a>-wielding Lothric Knight and several Murkmen. Drop onto the ash pile below and clear the area, the Miracle will be on a corpse behind a summoning Murkman.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster fires an orb that heals everything in its vicinity upon hitting a surface. Has the same animation as <a data-e=\"emit-force\">Emit Force<\/a>. All allied players affected by the spell will be healed for 1.7 times the Spell Buff rating of the catalyst. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Projected_Heal"},{"id":"rapport","kind":"spell","name":"Rapport","page":"Rapport","img":"assets/img/Rapport.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":7000,"desc":"Advanced pyromancy of Quelana, a daughter of the Witch of Izalith.\nCharms the enemy, making them temporary ally.\nThe living are lured by flame, and this tendency is elemental to the art of pyromancy.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 7,000 souls after she has been given the <a data-e=\"quelana-pyromancy-tome\">Quelana Pyromancy Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>At range, this spell turns a regular enemy into a friendly ally for 30 seconds. The spell takes two seconds to cast and can miss fast enemies but has considerable range, as it works by firing a small, invisible projectile straight forward.<\/p><p>The spell has no effect on other enemies, bosses, invaders or other players. However, there is no limit to the number of creatures that can be converted.<\/p><p>Whilst under Rapport, the targeted enemy:<\/p><ul><li>Will stop attacking the player and any allies they have.<\/li><li>Will be considered as an ally for spells that affect allies.<\/li><li>Cannot be targeted with lock-on.<\/li><li>Can be backstabbed.<\/li><li>Can still harm the player during their attack targeting other enemies.<\/li><li>Will attack invaders.<\/li><\/ul>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Rapport"},{"id":"repair","kind":"spell","name":"Repair","page":"Repair (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Repair__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"20","req":{"int":15,"fth":null},"buy":2000,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden sorceries.\nRepairs equipped weapons and armor. Includes weapons with exhausted durability.\nWhile the effects of this spell are rather subtle, its foundations are a well-guarded secret. Light is time, and the reversal of its effects is a forbidden art.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 2,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores 50 durability to all currently equipped weapons and armor, including weapons not currently being wielded. This applies to equipment that has been completely broken as well (e.g., has 0 durability).<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Repair_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"replenishment","kind":"spell","name":"Replenishment","page":"Replenishment (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Replenishment__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"30","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":1000,"desc":"Miracle once cherished by cleric knights. Gradually restores HP.\nReplenishment is a relic of the old Lloyd faith, whose cleric knights were unfaltering in battle.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores 5 HP per second for 58-59 seconds, for a total of 290-295 HP.<\/p><p>The duration of the heal, and thus amount of HP recovered, cannot be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Replenishment_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"sacred-flame","kind":"spell","name":"Sacred Flame","page":"Sacred Flame","img":"assets/img/Sacred_Flame.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":8,"fth":8},"buy":null,"desc":"Pyromancy taught among savages. Flame burrows inside foes and ignites.\nOriginally used in a ceremony for cleansing sacrificial impurities, thereby lending the spell its name.\nAs barbaric as it seems, this may in fact be quite fitting for the savage pyromancers who consider themselves servants of the divine.","avail":"<p>Found inside a lava pool in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>. Make way through the level until reaching the lowermost floor, past the area with several Basilisks and where Knight Slayer Tsorig attacks. The Sacred Flame lies on the left wall among the lava, the other item being an <a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a flame in their catalyst hand, then lunges forward in a grabbing motion. If it successfully connects with a valid target, it will place them in a riposte-like state, where the caster is granted invulnerability frames for the duration of the attack animation.<\/p><p>The caster thrusts the flame into the target, inflicting 0.3 times the Attack Rating of the catalyst as Fire damage. The flame then burns the target for 9 more instances of damage, each inflicting 0.1 times the Attack Rating of the catalyst as Fire damage. Finally, the flame explodes, knocking the target down and inflicting a critical amount of damage. The standard <a data-e=\"pyromancy-flame\">Pyromancy Flame<\/a> will inflict 2.3 times the Attack Rating of the catalyst as critical damage, the <a data-e=\"pyromancers-parting-flame\">Pyromancer's Parting Flame<\/a> will inflict 2.5 times the Attack Rating of the catalyst for an increase of 9% in damage over the standard Pyromancy Flame (while not inflicting the bonus Combustion damage), and the <a data-e=\"demons-scar\">Demon's Scar<\/a> will inflict 20% more damage for a 2.76 multiplier. The <a data-e=\"white-hair-talisman\">White Hair Talisman<\/a> inflicts its physical component as Thrust damage, as well as its Fire component, both using the 2.3 multiplier.<\/p><p>If a non-valid target is hit by the spell (one that cannot be placed into a riposte state), they will instead take two smaller instances of damage instead. Attempting to hit a valid target but failing due to terrain elevation differences will result in only dealing the initial grab damage.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sacred_Flame"},{"id":"sacred-oath","kind":"spell","name":"Sacred Oath","page":"Sacred Oath (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Sacred_Oath__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"65","req":{"int":null,"fth":28},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle of those chosen by the Sunlight covenant.\nTemporarily boosts attack and damage absorption for self and those in the vicinity.\nThis is the tale of the Sun's firstborn, his faithful first knight, and the brave dragonslayer who served them both.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 1 in the <a data-e=\"warrior-of-sunlight\">Warrior of Sunlight<\/a> covenant.<\/p>","use":"<p>Increases damage absorption by 10% across the board, while also increasing damage dealt with all weapons and spells by 10%, for 60 seconds. In PvP, the effects are 5% absorption and 5% damage bonus.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sacred_Oath_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"seek-guidance","kind":"spell","name":"Seek Guidance","page":"Seek Guidance (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Seek_Guidance__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":null,"fth":12},"buy":null,"desc":"Miracle of stray souls.\nDisplays more help from other worlds and reveals summon signs without using an ember.\nFaith serves as a guide for clerics, meaning they should have no need for secondhand wisdom. Be that as it may, this miracle has been passed down from soul to soul, providing a tiny ray of hope for the lost.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"cathedral-of-the-deep\">Cathedral of the Deep<\/a>. Head past the first Giant Slave on the second floor and take the path on the left after descending a small set of stairs. Follow this path to the end to reach a corpse holding the miracle under a Writhing Rotten Flesh.<\/p>","use":"<p>Displays extra messages, as well as developer-set messages. Reveals the location of summon signs without the use of an <a data-e=\"ember\">Ember<\/a>.<\/p><p>Does not allow the player to summon phantoms while unembered.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Seek_Guidance_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"seething-chaos","kind":"spell","name":"Seething Chaos","page":"Seething Chaos","img":"assets/img/Seething_Chaos.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"28","req":{"int":18,"fth":18},"buy":10000,"desc":"The last flame lit by the demon prince.\nThis pyromancy hurls a clump of chaos.\nUpon impact, this clump of chaos seethes wildly, condenses briefly, then explodes violently.\nTo the demons, these clumps are shreds of life.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-demon-prince\">Soul of the Demon Prince<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 10,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a fragment of the Flame of Chaos, then tosses it in the aimed direction. If the projectile makes contact with an enemy or destructible level geometry (tables, chairs, boxes, etc.), it will impact and stagger, deal 2.0 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage. However, if it lands on solid level geometry such as a floor or wall, it will attach to it and begin seething and growing in strength. Roughly 4.5 seconds after initial contact with the surface, it will explode, dealing 3.92 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Fire damage in an area.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Seething_Chaos"},{"id":"snap-freeze","kind":"spell","name":"Snap Freeze","page":"Snap Freeze","img":"assets/img/Snap_Freeze.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"16","req":{"int":18,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"One of the spells left behind by the young sorcerer Sulyvahn before leaving the Painted World. Creates a cloud of near-freezing mist.\nSulyvahn was born and raised inside the painting, yet had little use for his frigid homeland, since he had not yet experienced loss.","avail":"<p>Located after the Depth of the Painting bonfire. Run to the left past the Great Crab and it will be on a corpse behind a Birch Woman.<\/p>","use":"<p>Creates a cloud of freezing mist, rapidly inflicting 15 Frost buildup per tick on enemies within. Cloud persists for 5 seconds, and the duration cannot be extended by equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Snap_Freeze"},{"id":"soothing-sunlight","kind":"spell","name":"Soothing Sunlight","page":"Soothing Sunlight (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Soothing_Sunlight__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"80","req":{"int":null,"fth":45},"buy":5000,"desc":"Special miracle granted to the maidens of the Princess of Sunlight.\nRestores a large amount of HP for self and those in the general area.\nThe miracles of Gwynevere, the princess cherished by all, bestow their blessing on a great many warriors.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-dancer\">Soul of the Dancer<\/a> and 5,000 souls with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Restores HP for the caster and allies within the general area equal to 7 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst, and consumes 205 stamina. For catalysts that also scale with Intelligence such as <a data-e=\"crystal-chime\">Crystal Chime<\/a> and <a data-e=\"sunless-talisman\">Sunless Talisman<\/a>, only the Spell Buff from Faith is taken into account.<\/p><p>Due to the high stamina cost of this spell, action after casting is severely restricted, preventing the caster from rolling or attacking immediately after.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-the-dancer","cost":"5,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soothing_Sunlight_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-arrow","kind":"spell","name":"Soul Arrow","page":"Soul Arrow (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Soul_Arrow__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"7","req":{"int":10,"fth":null},"buy":"Varies","desc":"Elementary sorcery.\nFires a soul arrow.\nTo use sorceries, equip a staff and attune a sorcery at a bonfire.","avail":"<ul><li>Starting equipment for the Sorcerer class.<\/li><li>Sold by the <a data-e=\"shrine-handmaid\">Shrine Handmaid<\/a> for 2,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> (or <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a> after his death) for 1,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 1,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The most basic form of Soul Arrow. Fires a soul arrow at the target, dealing 1.27 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. Has a fast casting time. <br><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_Arrow_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-greatsword","kind":"spell","name":"Soul Greatsword","page":"Soul Greatsword (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Soul_Greatsword__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"23","req":{"int":22,"fth":null},"buy":5000,"desc":"Sorcery developed for sorcerer-swordsman. Attacks with a greatsword formed from souls.\nThe ephemeral blade only exists as an extension of the caster, but its power is said to rival that of physical greatswords. Even the most obstinate magic purists may resort to this spell in times of crisis.","avail":"<ul><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"yoel-of-londor\">Yoel of Londor<\/a> (or <a data-e=\"yuria-of-londor\">Yuria of Londor<\/a>) for 5,000 souls.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for the same price.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>Forms a soul greatsword after a short delay, then swings it in a wide arc in front of the caster, dealing 2.0 times the Spell Buff of the wielded catalyst as Magic damage to all enemies struck.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_Greatsword_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-spear","kind":"spell","name":"Soul Spear","page":"Soul Spear (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Soul_Spear__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"32","req":{"int":32,"fth":null},"buy":5000,"desc":"Sorcery developed by Big Hat Logan, the great sorcerer who left the Dragon School in an age long past.\nFires a soul spear.\nThe spear boasts superior penetrating power, and is testament to Logan's strength in battle.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 5,000 souls once he has been given <a data-e=\"logans-scroll\">Logan's Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Fires a soul spear at the target, dealing 2.5 times the catalyst's Spell Buff as Magic damage. The spear has a relatively short cast time and high travel speed, being capable of penetrating its target and hitting multiple foes at once if they are standing close together.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_Spear_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"soul-stream","kind":"spell","name":"Soul Stream","page":"Soul Stream","img":"assets/img/Soul_Stream.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":2,"fp":"55","req":{"int":45,"fth":null},"buy":null,"desc":"Sorcery imparted by the first of the Scholars, when Lothric and the Grand Archives were but young.\nFires a torrential volley of souls.\nThe first of the Scholars doubted the linking of the fire, and was alleged to be a private mentor to the Royal Prince.","avail":"<p>Found on the corpse of a sitting scholar in a short hallway beyond the Boreal Outrider Knight that is hidden behind an illusory wall on the fourth floor of the <a data-e=\"grand-archives\">Grand Archives<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Soul Stream is notable in that it is the only Sorcery that requires two Attunement slots.<\/p><p>The caster charges their catalyst with power for a few seconds in preparation for firing the spell; during this time, it is possible to walk slowly to change position and aiming direction. Once charging is complete, a wide beam of powerful soul energy is unleashed, inflicting extreme amounts of Magic damage to any enemies caught within its path.<\/p><p>For the duration of the attack, no movement is possible. The stream inflicts 6 instances of damage throughout the attack, as well as stagger and knockdown on enemies caught within; each damage instance will deal between 0.8 to 1.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Magic damage, increasing in strength with each successive instance. Combined, all 6 damage instances will deal the most amount of raw damage of any Sorcery in the game.<\/p><p>The beam has a relatively long effect range, roughly the same range as a <a data-e=\"soul-spear\">Soul Spear<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Soul_Stream"},{"id":"spook","kind":"spell","name":"Spook","page":"Spook","img":"assets/img/Spook.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":10,"fth":null},"buy":2000,"desc":"Sorcery developed by a certain surreptitious sorcerer at Vinheim Dragon School.\nMasks noises of the caster and prevents fall damage.\nTheir mastery of this sorcery alone allows Vinheim spooks to demand handsome payment for their services.","avail":"<ul><li>Part of the Assassin class starting equipment.<\/li><li>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> in <a data-e=\"firelink-shrine\">Firelink Shrine<\/a> for 2,000 souls.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<ul><li>Spook is one of the four Sorceries required to purchase, in order for Orbeck to bestow the <a data-e=\"slumbering-dragoncrest-ring\">Slumbering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a> and &quot;Silent Ally&quot; gesture.<\/li><\/ul><p><br><\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Spook"},{"id":"sunlight-spear","kind":"spell","name":"Sunlight Spear","page":"Sunlight Spear (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Sunlight_Spear__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"48","req":{"int":null,"fth":40},"buy":10000,"desc":"Miracle of Gwyn, the First Lord.\nHurls a sunlight spear.\nThe tales of Gwyn's Archdragon hunts describe the inception of the Age of Fire.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-the-lords\">Soul of the Lords<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 10,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>The strongest variant of the <a data-e=\"lightning-spear\">Lightning Spear<\/a> family of Miracles. Conjures a deep-colored spear made of Lightning, then hurls it at the target. The projectile inflicts 2.6 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage.<\/p><p>When cast at extremely close range, the spear will inflict an additional 1.9 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as Lightning damage. A successful point-blank cast will also result in vibration feedback through the player's controller, providing confirmation of inflicting additional damage.<\/p><p>While extremely damaging, Sunlight Spear is also very costly in terms of FP.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-the-lords","cost":null}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Sunlight_Spear_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"tears-of-denial","kind":"spell","name":"Tears of Denial","page":"Tears of Denial","img":"assets/img/Tears_of_Denial.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"100","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":10000,"desc":"Miracle taught by Morne, the Archbishop's apostle.\nGrants one chance to endure when HP reaches 0.\nIntended to grant the dying a few moments for a final farewell. Tears are shed for the sake of the living, more so than the deceased.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina of Carim<\/a> for 10,000 souls once she has been given the <a data-e=\"braille-divine-tome-of-carim\">Braille Divine Tome of Carim<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>When Tears of Denial is in effect, it will allow the player to survive a single killing blow, leaving them at 1 HP.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Tears_of_Denial"},{"id":"toxic-mist","kind":"spell","name":"Toxic Mist","page":"Toxic Mist (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Toxic_Mist__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":1,"fp":"24","req":{"int":null,"fth":15},"buy":null,"desc":"Unique pyromancy of Eingyi that never gained currency in the Great Swamp.\nCreates an intense poison mist.\nDriven from the Great Swamp, they say that at the end of his journey, Eingyi happened upon a virulent poison and a young lady.","avail":"<p>Found in the <a data-e=\"smouldering-lake\">Smouldering Lake<\/a>, on a corpse in a lava pool located behind an illusory wall in a room with three Hound Rats in it. After the exit to the right in the hallway with the Smouldering Ghru, it will be down some stairs on the left-hand side and is found on the visible first corpse.<\/p><p>In order to survive the trip inside the lava, there are many strategies that can be followed and combined before venturing inside. The main idea is to slow down the loss of HP enough to allow the player to heal and advance a bit further, until they have successfully retrieved the item and returned to solid ground.<\/p><p>Possible survival techniques include:<\/p><ul><li>Wearing pieces of armor that each provide the best Fire resistance from all other armor collected so far.<\/li><li>Making sure one is a Host of Embers in order to have a larger HP pool, thus having a better chance of surviving between heals.<\/li><li>Casting <a data-e=\"flash-sweat\">Flash Sweat<\/a>.<\/li><li>Consuming a <a data-e=\"red-bug-pellet\">Red Bug Pellet<\/a>.<\/li><li>Equipping rings that provide useful effects, such as:<ul><li><a data-e=\"flame-stoneplate-ring\">Flame Stoneplate Ring<\/a> (increases Fire resistance)<\/li><li><a data-e=\"estus-ring\">Estus Ring<\/a> (gives 20% more HP when drinking from the <a data-e=\"estus-flask\">Estus Flask<\/a>)<\/li><li><a data-e=\"chloranthy-ring\">Chloranthy Ring<\/a> (increases stamina regeneration rate)<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Equipping gear that provides HP regeneration, like the <a data-e=\"sun-princess-ring\">Sun Princess Ring<\/a> and the <a data-e=\"ancient-dragon-greatshield\">Ancient Dragon Greatshield<\/a>.<\/li><\/ul>","use":"<p>The caster reels back, then exhales a deep cloud of toxic mist, inflicting 12 Toxic buildup per tick to foes that stand in it. The cloud persists for 6 seconds.<\/p><p>Buildup is static and is not affected by rings or spell buffs.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Toxic_Mist_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"twisted-wall-of-light","kind":"spell","name":"Twisted Wall of Light","page":"Twisted Wall of Light","img":"assets/img/Twisted_Wall_of_Light.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"10","req":{"int":27,"fth":null},"buy":6000,"desc":"Lost sorcery from Oolacile, land of ancient golden sorceries. Distorts light in order to deflect magic.\nA closely-guarded light manipulation spell that contorts the very fabric of fundamental laws, negating magic by denying its claim to physicality.","avail":"<p>Sold by <a data-e=\"orbeck-of-vinheim\">Orbeck of Vinheim<\/a> for 6,000 souls once he has been given the <a data-e=\"golden-scroll\">Golden Scroll<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Deflects any magic attacks made against the player, similar to a Spell Parry.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Twisted_Wall_of_Light"},{"id":"vow-of-silence","kind":"spell","name":"Vow of Silence","page":"Vow of Silence (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Vow_of_Silence__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"35","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":15000,"desc":"Miracle of the Sable Church of Londor.\nPrevents spells in the vicinity, including one's own.\nMembers of the Sable Church are all trained swordsmen, each sworn only to their weapons as they bear the leaden silence of Londor.","avail":"<p>Sold by either <a data-e=\"irina-of-carim\">Irina<\/a> or <a data-e=\"karla\">Karla<\/a> for 15,000 souls after giving one of them the <a data-e=\"londor-braille-divine-tome\">Londor Braille Divine Tome<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>Prevents usage of magic in the area, including the caster, for 15 seconds.<\/p><p>Duration is increased on affected targets if they are wearing a <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>. This applies to the one who casts this miracle as well.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Vow_of_Silence_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"warmth","kind":"spell","name":"Warmth","page":"Warmth (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Warmth__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Pyromancy","slots":2,"fp":"50","req":{"int":null,"fth":25},"buy":null,"desc":"Peculiar pyromancy of the Mound-makers. Creates a gentle flame that restores HP on touch.\nThey feared separation from the gods and sought a familial bond, perhaps leading to the creation of this flame of harmony.","avail":"<p>Obtained as a reward for reaching Rank 2 in the <a data-e=\"mound-makers\">Mound-makers<\/a> covenant. To achieve this, the player is required to offer 30 <a data-e=\"vertebra-shackle\">Vertebra Shackles<\/a> to the altar in the <a data-e=\"undead-settlement\">Pit of Hollows<\/a>.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster conjures a floating flame that gradually heals all entities within its radius, regardless of affiliation. This includes the caster, allies and enemies. While under the flame's effect, entities will recover 35 HP per tick. The spell ticks once per second and lasts for 60 seconds, resulting in a maximum of 2,100 HP restored.<\/p><p>Only one instance of Warmth can be active at a time, as casting the spell before the previous instance expires will cause the previous flame to disappear, being replaced by the new one. The duration of the flame cannot be increased via equipping the <a data-e=\"lingering-dragoncrest-ring\">Lingering Dragoncrest Ring<\/a>.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Warmth_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"way-of-white-corona","kind":"spell","name":"Way of White Corona","page":"Way of White Corona","img":"assets/img/Way_of_White_Corona.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":1,"fp":"15","req":{"int":null,"fth":18},"buy":null,"desc":"A lost Way of White miracle. Launches a white discus which slices into foes and returns to the conjurer.\nLong ago, when the imprints left by the gods were still deep, miracles of the Way of White existed alongside aureoles.\nThose who yearned for the long-lost aureoles fully believed that they would return, one day.","avail":"<p>Found inside a chapel near the end of the Corvian Settlement, after ascending to the top of the settlement and traversing a cliff-side then dropping into the building. It is guarded by two Corvian Knights, one of each variant.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster quickly conjures a white discus and launches it forward. The discus deals 0.85 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as  physical damage.<\/p><p>The disc will be destroyed upon hitting any solid level geometry, such as walls and floors. If it travels the full distance it will hover in place, dealing damage up to 3 times at its location, before returning to the caster, also inflicting damage as it returns. Thus, including the travel forward and back, Way of White Corona can inflict up to 5 instances of damage in a single cast. Multiple instances of this Miracle can be active at once.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Way_of_White_Corona"},{"id":"white-dragon-breath","kind":"spell","name":"White Dragon Breath","page":"White Dragon Breath (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/White_Dragon_Breath__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Sorcery","slots":1,"fp":"25","req":{"int":50,"fth":null},"buy":10000,"desc":"Sorcery of the deluded Consumed King Oceiros.\nEmits crystal breath of Seath the Scaleless.\nCrystal breath has piercing qualities.\nSeath's research seemed to strike a chord with old Big Hat who, in his mad, disrobed state, made divine works such as this, his own. Oceiros was no doubt edified by this.","avail":"<p>Obtained by transposing the <a data-e=\"soul-of-consumed-oceiros\">Soul of Consumed Oceiros<\/a> with <a data-e=\"ludleth-of-courland\">Ludleth of Courland<\/a> for 10,000 souls.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster charges and then fires a beam from their staff, forming a vertical line of crystals on the ground in front. Anything standing in the path of the beam as the crystals form will take Magic damage equal to 2.65 times the Spell Buff of the caster's catalyst.<\/p>","from_soul":[{"soul":"soul-of-consumed-oceiros","cost":"10,000 souls"}],"url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/White_Dragon_Breath_(Dark_Souls_III)"},{"id":"wrath-of-the-gods","kind":"spell","name":"Wrath of the Gods","page":"Wrath of the Gods (Dark Souls III)","img":"assets/img/Wrath_of_the_Gods__Dark_Souls_III.webp","school":"Miracle","slots":2,"fp":"40","req":{"int":null,"fth":30},"buy":null,"desc":"Primal form of Force. Creates a powerful shockwave.\nWrath of the Gods is an epic tale, while Force is but a woefully incomplete version of that yarn.\nThis primal account of profound fury emits a shockwave that also inflicts damage.","avail":"<p>Found within the <a data-e=\"profaned-capital\">Profaned Capital<\/a>. In the area with the toxic swamp, climb up to the roof of the main building. There will be a hole in the wall, next to the Court Sorcerer. Drop down to find the spell on a corpse.<\/p>","use":"<p>The caster charges themselves with energy, and then releases it in an explosive shockwave centered around the caster. While the spell is charging, the caster can slowly walk and hold it at the ready. The explosion inflicts 3.2 times the Spell Buff of the catalyst as physical damage, and knocks down any enemies caught by it.<\/p><p>Due to the moderately slow casting time, it is recommended that a talisman be used to cast as they have the Unfaltering Prayer skill, which grants the user temporary Hyper Armor and thus greatly decreases the chances of the spell being interrupted. The <a data-e=\"sunlight-talisman\">Sunlight Talisman<\/a> provides the strongest poise in its skill.<\/p>","url":"https://darksouls.fandom.com/wiki/Wrath_of_the_Gods_(Dark_Souls_III)"}]);
